window.MG_LAZY_DATA["data/lazy/courses/b115-abf1e4c3d07c6e9b.json"]={sha256:"abf1e4c3d07c6e9b8fe39ba04d039560e356f3c0ba04ce4f6a034aa928605292",value:{"id":"b115","title":"弗雷瑞斯公路隧道","titleEn":"Frejus Road Tunnel","category":"underground","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","summary":"法國交通主管機關列弗雷瑞斯原隧道12.87公里、1980年營運，並於2025年公告第二孔開通活動。本課不把原始單孔狀態當成永久現況，而以新舊孔轉換為主軸，研究重車交通、岩體、通風隔離、跨孔救援與設備版本，建立分階段可驗證的營運模型。","summaryEn":"The French transport ministry records the original Frejus tunnel as 12.87 km, in service from 1980, and announced the second-tube opening event in 2025. The course does not treat the original single-bore arrangement as permanent. It studies staged transfer, freight traffic, rock behaviour, airflow isolation, cross-bore rescue and equipment revisions.","scope":"依公開工程原理、官方資料與規範架構編寫的原創教學；步驟是可驗證的學習任務與假想算例，不是設計圖說、施工計畫、開挖、注漿或受限空間作業許可，也不是任何專案的設計文件。數值均為教學假設或公開資料，實際工程須由合格技師依規範與實測資料重新計算並簽證。","scopeEn":"Original teaching built from public engineering principles, official sources and code frameworks. Steps are verifiable learning tasks and hypothetical exercises, not design drawings, method statements, excavation, grouting or confined-space permits, or any project's design documents. Numbers are teaching assumptions or public data; real work must be recalculated and certified by qualified engineers using codes and measured data.","subcategory":"ug-landmarks","subcategoryTitle":"世界隧道與地下巨作","subcategoryTitleEn":"World tunnels and underground landmarks","learningTrack":"underground","learningSubdiscipline":"ug-landmarks","learningTags":["underground","ug-landmarks","tunnel"],"architectureFamily":"tunnel","architectureNodes":[["路線里程與端點","Alignment chainage and endpoints"],["破碎帶連通性","Fault-zone connectivity"],["支護安裝時點","Support activation time"],["風道摩擦壓損","Duct friction loss"],["所需疏散時間","Required evacuation time"],["資產資料完整度","Asset-record completeness"]],"architectureEdges":[[0,1],[1,2],[2,3],[3,4],[4,5],[1,5]],"diagram":{"type":"tunnel","labels":["路線里程與端點","破碎帶連通性","支護安裝時點","風道摩擦壓損","所需疏散時間"],"labelsEn":["Alignment chainage and endpoints","Fault-zone connectivity","Support activation time","Duct friction loss","Required evacuation time"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"workedExample":{"title":"原創假想算例與邊界","titleEn":"Original hypothetical example and boundaries","text":"原創綜合審查：先計算「破碎帶連通與預報更新」，再獨立計算「通風網路與壓力損失」。原創教學假設：滲透係數=5e-06 m/s；水力坡降=2.1 無因次；通水面積=340 m²。Q=k i A=0.00357 m³/s。僅把滲透係數增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為0.003927 m³/s。邊界：均質飽和達西流，不代表裂隙集中流；不是本工程實測或允收值。原創教學假設：達西因子=0.025 無因次；風道長度=1060 m；水力直徑=4 m；空氣密度=1.2 kg/m³；平均風速=3.5 m/s。Δp=f(L/D)ρv²/2=48.6937 Pa。僅把平均風速增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為58.9194 Pa。邊界：定密度直管摩阻，局部損失及外風另計；不是本工程實測或允收值。兩組結果的單位與邊界不同，不能直接相加。請列出一項缺少的現場輸入，說明它會影響哪個結論，以及哪種獨立量測可以縮小不確定度。","textEn":"Original integrated review: first calculate fault connectivity and forecast updating, then independently calculate ventilation network and pressure loss. Original teaching assumptions: conductivity=5e-06 m/s; hydraulic gradient=2.1 dimensionless; flow area=340 m². Q=k i A=0.00357 m³/s. Increasing only conductivity by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 0.003927 m³/s. Boundary: Homogeneous saturated Darcy flow, not concentrated fracture flow. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Original teaching assumptions: Darcy factor=0.025 dimensionless; duct length=1060 m; hydraulic diameter=4 m; air density=1.2 kg/m³; mean velocity=3.5 m/s. Δp=f(L/D)ρv²/2=48.6937 Pa. Increasing only mean velocity by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 58.9194 Pa. Boundary: Constant-density straight-duct friction; local loss and external wind are separate. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. The outputs have different units and boundaries and cannot simply be added. Identify one missing field input, explain which conclusion it changes and select an independent measurement to reduce uncertainty.","assumptions":"數值是本課自行設定的教學假設，不代表任何專案的設計值、量測值或規範允許值；改變系統邊界或荷載組合後必須重算。","assumptionsEn":"Inputs are teaching assumptions, not any project's design values, measurements or code allowances; recalculate after changing the system boundary or load combination.","sourceScope":"原創數值練習；來源支援公開原理與工程背景，不宣稱來源提供這組數據。","sourceScopeEn":"Original numerical exercise; sources support public principles and project context, not these numbers."},"depth":5,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"simulationOnly":true,"educationEdition":14,"enrichmentVersion":14,"stages":[{"id":"b115-v14-s1","title":"地層條件、邊界與工程系統","titleEn":"Ground conditions, boundaries and engineering system","description":"本階段聚焦「服務邊界與路線代價」與「破碎帶連通與預報更新」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Service boundaries and alignment cost\" and \"Fault connectivity and forecast updating\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b115-v14-01","title":"服務邊界與路線代價：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Service boundaries and alignment cost: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"objective":"說明「路線里程與端點」如何影響弗雷瑞斯公路隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Alignment chainage and endpoints” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Frejus Road Tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"弗雷瑞斯由原孔到第二孔的配置變化需先定義階段，教材把道路容量、救援通道和施工空間分開。隧道選線同時改變洞口、覆土與縱坡，短路線不保證低地質風險。比較方案必須使用相同起訖點，並分開主孔、引道及服務坑的工程數量；交通時間只是需求的一個指標，不能代替施工可達性或長期維修評估。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「路線里程與端點」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Define configuration stages before comparing the original and second tubes, separating road capacity, rescue access and construction space. Alignment changes portals, cover and gradient together, so a shorter tunnel need not have lower geological risk. Compare options between identical endpoints and distinguish running bores, approaches and service galleries. Travel time measures one service benefit but cannot replace assessment of construction access, maintenance closures or exposure to uncertain ground. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Alignment chainage and endpoints” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：長度=17.6 km；速度=60 km/h。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: length=17.6 km; speed=60 km/h. t=60L/v=17.6 min.","failure":"常見誤解：「最短的隧道路線一定也有最低施工與維護風險。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"The shortest tunnel alignment necessarily has the lowest construction and maintenance risk.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「路線里程與端點」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Alignment chainage and endpoints”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b115-v14-01-k1","title":"服務邊界與路線代價","titleEn":"Service boundaries and alignment cost","text":"弗雷瑞斯由原孔到第二孔的配置變化需先定義階段，教材把道路容量、救援通道和施工空間分開。隧道選線同時改變洞口、覆土與縱坡，短路線不保證低地質風險。","textEn":"Define configuration stages before comparing the original and second tubes, separating road capacity, rescue access and construction space. Alignment changes portals, cover and gradient together, so a shorter tunnel need not have lower geological risk.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b115-v14-01-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：最短的隧道路線一定也有最低施工與維護風險。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: The shortest tunnel alignment necessarily has the lowest construction and maintenance risk. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「服務邊界與路線代價」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Service boundaries and alignment cost\" is correct?","options":["最短的隧道路線一定也有最低施工與維護風險。","弗雷瑞斯由原孔到第二孔的配置變化需先定義階段，教材把道路容量、救援通道和施工空間分開。","岩芯很硬就可以排除破碎帶變形與集中湧水。"],"optionsEn":["The shortest tunnel alignment necessarily has the lowest construction and maintenance risk.","Define configuration stages before comparing the original and second tubes, separating road capacity, rescue access and construction space.","Hard intact core excludes fault-zone deformation and concentrated inflow."],"answer":1,"explanation":"弗雷瑞斯由原孔到第二孔的配置變化需先定義階段，教材把道路容量、救援通道和施工空間分開。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Define configuration stages before comparing the original and second tubes, separating road capacity, rescue access and construction space. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":1},{"id":"b115-v14-02","title":"服務邊界與路線代價：定量估算","titleEn":"Service boundaries and alignment cost: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b115-v14-01"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「路線里程與端點」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Alignment chainage and endpoints” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：長度=17.6 km；速度=60 km/h。t=60L/v=17.6 min。僅把長度增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為19.36 min。邊界：假想交通旅程，未含加減速、排隊及實際時刻表；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: length=17.6 km; speed=60 km/h. t=60L/v=17.6 min. Increasing only length by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 19.36 min. Boundary: Hypothetical transport journey excluding acceleration, queues and the real timetable. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：每個方案附日期和孔別，不混用不同時期示意圖。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Attach dates and bore identifiers to each option and avoid mixing historical diagrams.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b115-v14-02-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：長度=17.6 km；速度=60 km/h。t=60L/v=17.6 min。僅把長度增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為19.36 min。邊界：假想交通旅程，未含加減速、排隊及實際時刻表；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: length=17.6 km; speed=60 km/h. t=60L/v=17.6 min. Increasing only length by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 19.36 min. Boundary: Hypothetical transport journey excluding acceleration, queues and the real timetable. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b115-v14-02-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「服務邊界與路線代價」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Service boundaries and alignment cost\", which statement holds?","options":["支護越厚越硬就一定能解決所有擠壓性地層。","風機銘牌風量相加就是全隧道各處可用的通風量。","原創教學假設：長度=17.6 km；速度=60 km/h。"],"optionsEn":["Thicker and stiffer support necessarily solves every squeezing-ground problem.","Adding fan nameplate flows gives the usable airflow everywhere in the tunnel.","Original teaching assumptions: length=17.6 km; speed=60 km/h. t=60L/v=17.6 min."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設：長度=17.6 km；速度=60 km/h。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: length=17.6 km; speed=60 km/h. t=60L/v=17.6 min. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":2},{"id":"b115-v14-03","title":"服務邊界與路線代價：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Service boundaries and alignment cost: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b115-v14-02"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「路線里程與端點」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Alignment chainage and endpoints” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"每個方案附日期和孔別，不混用不同時期示意圖。把縱斷面、地形與地質剖面疊合，以端點坐標獨立反算距離，再將主孔與支坑數量分開核對。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Attach dates and bore identifiers to each option and avoid mixing historical diagrams. Overlay the longitudinal profile, terrain and geology; independently derive distances from endpoint coordinates and reconcile running-bore and gallery quantities separately. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「路線里程與端點」的交付需回答：每個方案附日期和孔別，不混用不同時期示意圖。在方案表中凍結起訖點、計量範圍及地質假設，任何改線都要同步更新高程、數量與服務情境，不能只替換總長。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Frejus Road Tunnel, the alignment chainage and endpoints handover must address the following evidence: Attach dates and bore identifiers to each option and avoid mixing historical diagrams. Freeze endpoints, measurement scope and ground assumptions in the option register; realignment requires coordinated updates to elevations, quantities and service scenarios rather than replacing one length.","failure":"注意干擾：把舊單孔描述用於新配置會錯估對向衝突及逃生路線。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Applying an old single-bore description misstates opposing traffic and escape routes. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b115-v14-03-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"每個方案附日期和孔別，不混用不同時期示意圖。把縱斷面、地形與地質剖面疊合，以端點坐標獨立反算距離，再將主孔與支坑數量分開核對。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Attach dates and bore identifiers to each option and avoid mixing historical diagrams. Overlay the longitudinal profile, terrain and geology; independently derive distances from endpoint coordinates and reconcile running-bore and gallery quantities separately. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b115-v14-03-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「路線里程與端點」的交付需回答：每個方案附日期和孔別，不混用不同時期示意圖。在方案表中凍結起訖點、計量範圍及地質假設，任何改線都要同步更新高程、數量與服務情境，不能只替換總長。","textEn":"For Frejus Road Tunnel, the alignment chainage and endpoints handover must address the following evidence: Attach dates and bore identifiers to each option and avoid mixing historical diagrams. Freeze endpoints, measurement scope and ground assumptions in the option register; realignment requires coordinated updates to elevations, quantities and service scenarios rather than replacing one length.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「服務邊界與路線代價」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Service boundaries and alignment cost\"?","options":["每個方案附日期和孔別，不混用不同時期示意圖。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、開挖序列與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","只要出口距離短，就不需要比較可用與所需安全時間。"],"optionsEn":["Attach dates and bore identifiers to each option and avoid mixing historical diagrams.","Temperature, water head, excavation sequence and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","Short exit distance removes the need to compare available and required safe time."],"answer":0,"explanation":"每個方案附日期和孔別，不混用不同時期示意圖。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Attach dates and bore identifiers to each option and avoid mixing historical diagrams. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":3},{"id":"b115-v14-04","title":"服務邊界與路線代價：失效診斷","titleEn":"Service boundaries and alignment cost: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b115-v14-03"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「路線里程與端點」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Alignment chainage and endpoints” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"把舊單孔描述用於新配置會錯估對向衝突及逃生路線。混用全線與單孔長度會同時扭曲工程數量、行程及逃生距離，造成方案比較失去共同基準。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Applying an old single-bore description misstates opposing traffic and escape routes. Mixing whole-route and single-bore lengths distorts quantities, journey time and escape distance, destroying the common basis of an option comparison. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：比較方案必須使用相同起訖點，並分開主孔、引道及服務坑的工程數量；交通時間只是需求的一個指標，不能代替施工可達性或長期維修評估。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Travel time measures one service benefit but cannot replace assessment of construction access, maintenance closures or exposure to uncertain ground.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「最短的隧道路線一定也有最低施工與維護風險。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"The shortest tunnel alignment necessarily has the lowest construction and maintenance risk.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b115-v14-04-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"把舊單孔描述用於新配置會錯估對向衝突及逃生路線。混用全線與單孔長度會同時扭曲工程數量、行程及逃生距離，造成方案比較失去共同基準。","textEn":"Applying an old single-bore description misstates opposing traffic and escape routes. Mixing whole-route and single-bore lengths distorts quantities, journey time and escape distance, destroying the common basis of an option comparison.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b115-v14-04-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「服務邊界與路線代價」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Service boundaries and alignment cost\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","把舊單孔描述用於新配置會錯估對向衝突及逃生路線。","岩芯很硬就可以排除破碎帶變形與集中湧水。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Applying an old single-bore description misstates opposing traffic and escape routes.","Hard intact core excludes fault-zone deformation and concentrated inflow."],"answer":1,"explanation":"把舊單孔描述用於新配置會錯估對向衝突及逃生路線。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Applying an old single-bore description misstates opposing traffic and escape routes. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":4},{"id":"b115-v14-05","title":"破碎帶連通與預報更新：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Fault connectivity and forecast updating: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b115-v14-04"],"objective":"說明「破碎帶連通性」如何影響弗雷瑞斯公路隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Fault-zone connectivity” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Frejus Road Tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"平行第二孔可利用原孔資料但不能省略新探查，弗雷瑞斯教材研究斜交節理在兩孔位置的差異。斷層帶可以含很硬的岩塊，但整體變形與湧水常由填充節理和連通裂隙控制。單一岩芯強度不能代表整個掌子面；超前鑽孔、出水變化與揭露地質須回饋同一里程模型，預報則應保留不同情境及其證據權重。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「破碎帶連通性」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"The second tube can use first-bore records without replacing new investigation; examine oblique joints crossing each bore at different positions. A fault zone may contain strong intact blocks while filled joints and connected fractures govern its bulk deformation and inflow. One core strength does not represent the entire face. Probe records, water response and exposed geology must update a common chainage model, preserving competing interpretations and their evidential weight rather than treating a forecast as certainty. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Fault-zone connectivity” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：滲透係數=5e-06 m/s；水力坡降=2.1 無因次；通水面積=340 m²。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: conductivity=5e-06 m/s; hydraulic gradient=2.1 dimensionless; flow area=340 m².","failure":"常見誤解：「岩芯很硬就可以排除破碎帶變形與集中湧水。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Hard intact core excludes fault-zone deformation and concentrated inflow.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「破碎帶連通性」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Fault-zone connectivity”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b115-v14-05-k1","title":"破碎帶連通與預報更新","titleEn":"Fault connectivity and forecast updating","text":"平行第二孔可利用原孔資料但不能省略新探查，弗雷瑞斯教材研究斜交節理在兩孔位置的差異。斷層帶可以含很硬的岩塊，但整體變形與湧水常由填充節理和連通裂隙控制。","textEn":"The second tube can use first-bore records without replacing new investigation; examine oblique joints crossing each bore at different positions. A fault zone may contain strong intact blocks while filled joints and connected fractures govern its bulk deformation and inflow.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b115-v14-05-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：岩芯很硬就可以排除破碎帶變形與集中湧水。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Hard intact core excludes fault-zone deformation and concentrated inflow. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「破碎帶連通與預報更新」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Fault connectivity and forecast updating\" is correct?","options":["岩芯很硬就可以排除破碎帶變形與集中湧水。","知道覆土深度就能唯一決定洞壁各方向的應力。","平行第二孔可利用原孔資料但不能省略新探查，弗雷瑞斯教材研究斜交節理在兩孔位置的差異。"],"optionsEn":["Hard intact core excludes fault-zone deformation and concentrated inflow.","Cover depth uniquely determines wall stress in every direction.","The second tube can use first-bore records without replacing new investigation; examine oblique joints crossing each bore at different positions."],"answer":2,"explanation":"平行第二孔可利用原孔資料但不能省略新探查，弗雷瑞斯教材研究斜交節理在兩孔位置的差異。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"The second tube can use first-bore records without replacing new investigation; examine oblique joints crossing each bore at different positions. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":5},{"id":"b115-v14-06","title":"破碎帶連通與預報更新：定量估算","titleEn":"Fault connectivity and forecast updating: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b115-v14-05"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「破碎帶連通性」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Fault-zone connectivity” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：滲透係數=5e-06 m/s；水力坡降=2.1 無因次；通水面積=340 m²。Q=k i A=0.00357 m³/s。僅把滲透係數增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為0.003927 m³/s。邊界：均質飽和達西流，不代表裂隙集中流；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: conductivity=5e-06 m/s; hydraulic gradient=2.1 dimensionless; flow area=340 m². Q=k i A=0.00357 m³/s. Increasing only conductivity by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 0.003927 m³/s. Boundary: Homogeneous saturated Darcy flow, not concentrated fracture flow. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：將構造方位投影到兩孔里程，再用新揭露驗證。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Project structural orientation onto both chainages and test against new exposures.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b115-v14-06-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：滲透係數=5e-06 m/s；水力坡降=2.1 無因次；通水面積=340 m²。Q=k i A=0.00357 m³/s。僅把滲透係數增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為0.003927 m³/s。邊界：均質飽和達西流，不代表裂隙集中流；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: conductivity=5e-06 m/s; hydraulic gradient=2.1 dimensionless; flow area=340 m². Q=k i A=0.00357 m³/s. Increasing only conductivity by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 0.003927 m³/s. Boundary: Homogeneous saturated Darcy flow, not concentrated fracture flow. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b115-v14-06-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「破碎帶連通與預報更新」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Fault connectivity and forecast updating\", which statement holds?","options":["原創教學假設：滲透係數=5e-06 m/s；水力坡降=2.1 無因次；通水面積=340 m²。","混凝土強度達標就不必檢查接縫轉動與偏壓。","照度越高就必然使隧道內所有物體更容易辨識。"],"optionsEn":["Original teaching assumptions: conductivity=5e-06 m/s; hydraulic gradient=2.1 dimensionless; flow area=340 m².","Passing concrete strength eliminates the need to check joint rotation and uneven pressure.","Higher illuminance necessarily makes every tunnel object easier to detect."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創教學假設：滲透係數=5e-06 m/s；水力坡降=2.1 無因次；通水面積=340 m²。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: conductivity=5e-06 m/s; hydraulic gradient=2.1 dimensionless; flow area=340 m². Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":6},{"id":"b115-v14-07","title":"破碎帶連通與預報更新：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Fault connectivity and forecast updating: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b115-v14-06"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「破碎帶連通性」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Fault-zone connectivity” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"將構造方位投影到兩孔里程，再用新揭露驗證。將岩心回收、裂隙方位與出水曲線按里程對齊，用未參與建模的孔段作交叉檢驗，檢查是否只擬合已知資料。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Project structural orientation onto both chainages and test against new exposures. Align recovery, fracture orientation and inflow by chainage; test the interpretation against a withheld borehole interval to detect fitting only the known observations. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「破碎帶連通性」的交付需回答：將構造方位投影到兩孔里程，再用新揭露驗證。每次地質模型更新保留舊版與新增證據，差異由地質及支護設計者共同判讀，施工條件改變需重新確認核准範圍。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Frejus Road Tunnel, the fault-zone connectivity handover must address the following evidence: Project structural orientation onto both chainages and test against new exposures. Retain previous interpretations and new evidence at every update; geology and support designers jointly interpret differences and reconfirm approved bounds when ground conditions change.","failure":"注意干擾：按相同里程直接配對地質會忽略斜交造成的位置差。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Matching geology at equal chainage ignores offsets caused by oblique structures. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b115-v14-07-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"將構造方位投影到兩孔里程，再用新揭露驗證。將岩心回收、裂隙方位與出水曲線按里程對齊，用未參與建模的孔段作交叉檢驗，檢查是否只擬合已知資料。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Project structural orientation onto both chainages and test against new exposures. Align recovery, fracture orientation and inflow by chainage; test the interpretation against a withheld borehole interval to detect fitting only the known observations. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b115-v14-07-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「破碎帶連通性」的交付需回答：將構造方位投影到兩孔里程，再用新揭露驗證。每次地質模型更新保留舊版與新增證據，差異由地質及支護設計者共同判讀，施工條件改變需重新確認核准範圍。","textEn":"For Frejus Road Tunnel, the fault-zone connectivity handover must address the following evidence: Project structural orientation onto both chainages and test against new exposures. Retain previous interpretations and new evidence at every update; geology and support designers jointly interpret differences and reconfirm approved bounds when ground conditions change.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「破碎帶連通與預報更新」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Fault connectivity and forecast updating\"?","options":["沿用另一條隧道或另一處地層的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","將構造方位投影到兩孔里程，再用新揭露驗證。","設備有兩台就可以直接把各自故障率相乘判定安全。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another tunnel or ground formation counts as verifying this structure.","Project structural orientation onto both chainages and test against new exposures.","Two units allow their failure probabilities to be multiplied directly to establish safety."],"answer":1,"explanation":"將構造方位投影到兩孔里程，再用新揭露驗證。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Project structural orientation onto both chainages and test against new exposures. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":7},{"id":"b115-v14-08","title":"破碎帶連通與預報更新：失效診斷","titleEn":"Fault connectivity and forecast updating: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b115-v14-07"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「破碎帶連通性」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Fault-zone connectivity” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"按相同里程直接配對地質會忽略斜交造成的位置差。只用完整岩石強度會漏掉軟弱填充物，可能在看似堅硬的地層中出現收斂加快、支護過載或水量突增。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Matching geology at equal chainage ignores offsets caused by oblique structures. Intact strength alone misses weak infill, allowing accelerating convergence, support overload or sudden inflow in ground that superficially appears strong. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：單一岩芯強度不能代表整個掌子面；超前鑽孔、出水變化與揭露地質須回饋同一里程模型，預報則應保留不同情境及其證據權重。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Probe records, water response and exposed geology must update a common chainage model, preserving competing interpretations and their evidential weight rather than treating a forecast as certainty.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「岩芯很硬就可以排除破碎帶變形與集中湧水。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Hard intact core excludes fault-zone deformation and concentrated inflow.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b115-v14-08-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"按相同里程直接配對地質會忽略斜交造成的位置差。只用完整岩石強度會漏掉軟弱填充物，可能在看似堅硬的地層中出現收斂加快、支護過載或水量突增。","textEn":"Matching geology at equal chainage ignores offsets caused by oblique structures. Intact strength alone misses weak infill, allowing accelerating convergence, support overload or sudden inflow in ground that superficially appears strong.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b115-v14-08-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「破碎帶連通與預報更新」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Fault connectivity and forecast updating\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","知道覆土深度就能唯一決定洞壁各方向的應力。","按相同里程直接配對地質會忽略斜交造成的位置差。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","Cover depth uniquely determines wall stress in every direction.","Matching geology at equal chainage ignores offsets caused by oblique structures."],"answer":2,"explanation":"按相同里程直接配對地質會忽略斜交造成的位置差。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Matching geology at equal chainage ignores offsets caused by oblique structures. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":8}],"order":1},{"id":"b115-v14-s2","title":"機制、材料與定量設計","titleEn":"Mechanisms, materials and quantitative design","description":"本階段聚焦「覆土應力與洞壁重分配」與「支護啟動與變形容量」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Cover stress and wall redistribution\" and \"Support activation and deformation capacity\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b115-v14-09","title":"覆土應力與洞壁重分配：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Cover stress and wall redistribution: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b115-v14-08"],"objective":"說明「洞壁切向應力」如何影響弗雷瑞斯公路隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Tangential wall stress” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Frejus Road Tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"第二孔開挖與原孔營運並存時需檢查岩柱應力重分配，單孔覆土估算只是起點。開挖使岩體洞壁失去徑向拘束，遠場荷載轉移到周圍岩體，局部切向應力可能升高。圓孔彈性解可辨識量級，但節理、非圓斷面、塑性區與原位應力比會改變峰值位置，不能只用覆土重量推定全部三維應力。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「洞壁切向應力」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"When excavation coexists with first-bore operation, examine pillar stress redistribution beyond a single-hole cover estimate. Excavation removes radial confinement at the wall and transfers load through the surrounding rock, potentially raising local tangential stress. An elastic circular-hole solution identifies scale, but joints, noncircular geometry, yielding and the in-situ stress ratio alter the peak location. Cover weight alone cannot establish the complete three-dimensional stress state or support demand. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Tangential wall stress” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：覆土深度=920 m；岩體單位重=26 kN/m³。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: cover=920 m; rock unit weight=26 kN/m³. σθ,max=3γH/1000=71.76 MPa.","failure":"常見誤解：「知道覆土深度就能唯一決定洞壁各方向的應力。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Cover depth uniquely determines wall stress in every direction.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「洞壁切向應力」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Tangential wall stress”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b115-v14-09-k1","title":"覆土應力與洞壁重分配","titleEn":"Cover stress and wall redistribution","text":"第二孔開挖與原孔營運並存時需檢查岩柱應力重分配，單孔覆土估算只是起點。開挖使岩體洞壁失去徑向拘束，遠場荷載轉移到周圍岩體，局部切向應力可能升高。","textEn":"When excavation coexists with first-bore operation, examine pillar stress redistribution beyond a single-hole cover estimate. Excavation removes radial confinement at the wall and transfers load through the surrounding rock, potentially raising local tangential stress.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b115-v14-09-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：知道覆土深度就能唯一決定洞壁各方向的應力。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Cover depth uniquely determines wall stress in every direction. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「覆土應力與洞壁重分配」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Cover stress and wall redistribution\" is correct?","options":["第二孔開挖與原孔營運並存時需檢查岩柱應力重分配，單孔覆土估算只是起點。","知道覆土深度就能唯一決定洞壁各方向的應力。","支護越厚越硬就一定能解決所有擠壓性地層。"],"optionsEn":["When excavation coexists with first-bore operation, examine pillar stress redistribution beyond a single-hole cover estimate.","Cover depth uniquely determines wall stress in every direction.","Thicker and stiffer support necessarily solves every squeezing-ground problem."],"answer":0,"explanation":"第二孔開挖與原孔營運並存時需檢查岩柱應力重分配，單孔覆土估算只是起點。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"When excavation coexists with first-bore operation, examine pillar stress redistribution beyond a single-hole cover estimate. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":9},{"id":"b115-v14-10","title":"覆土應力與洞壁重分配：定量估算","titleEn":"Cover stress and wall redistribution: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b115-v14-09"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「洞壁切向應力」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Tangential wall stress” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：覆土深度=920 m；岩體單位重=26 kN/m³。σθ,max=3γH/1000=71.76 MPa。僅把覆土深度增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為78.936 MPa。邊界：無支承彈性圓孔，僅垂直遠場壓縮且水平遠場應力為零時，側壁最大環向壓應力；不是任意位置應力或完整三維原位解；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: cover=920 m; rock unit weight=26 kN/m³. σθ,max=3γH/1000=71.76 MPa. Increasing only cover by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 78.936 MPa. Boundary: Maximum tangential compression at the sidewalls of an unsupported elastic circular hole under vertical uniaxial remote loading with zero horizontal remote stress; not stress at any point or the complete three-dimensional in-situ state. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：把原孔位移與新掌子面距離對齊，排除溫度漂移。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Align old-bore movement with new-face distance while excluding thermal drift.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b115-v14-10-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：覆土深度=920 m；岩體單位重=26 kN/m³。σθ,max=3γH/1000=71.76 MPa。僅把覆土深度增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為78.936 MPa。邊界：無支承彈性圓孔，僅垂直遠場壓縮且水平遠場應力為零時，側壁最大環向壓應力；不是任意位置應力或完整三維原位解；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: cover=920 m; rock unit weight=26 kN/m³. σθ,max=3γH/1000=71.76 MPa. Increasing only cover by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 78.936 MPa. Boundary: Maximum tangential compression at the sidewalls of an unsupported elastic circular hole under vertical uniaxial remote loading with zero horizontal remote stress; not stress at any point or the complete three-dimensional in-situ state. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b115-v14-10-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「覆土應力與洞壁重分配」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Cover stress and wall redistribution\", which statement holds?","options":["風機銘牌風量相加就是全隧道各處可用的通風量。","原創教學假設：覆土深度=920 m；岩體單位重=26 kN/m³。","只要出口距離短，就不需要比較可用與所需安全時間。"],"optionsEn":["Adding fan nameplate flows gives the usable airflow everywhere in the tunnel.","Original teaching assumptions: cover=920 m; rock unit weight=26 kN/m³. σθ,max=3γH/1000=71.76 MPa.","Short exit distance removes the need to compare available and required safe time."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創教學假設：覆土深度=920 m；岩體單位重=26 kN/m³。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: cover=920 m; rock unit weight=26 kN/m³. σθ,max=3γH/1000=71.76 MPa. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":10},{"id":"b115-v14-11","title":"覆土應力與洞壁重分配：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Cover stress and wall redistribution: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b115-v14-10"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「洞壁切向應力」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Tangential wall stress” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"把原孔位移與新掌子面距離對齊，排除溫度漂移。將原位應力量測、岩石試驗及洞壁破壞方位相互比較，再用多點伸長計檢查變形是否與所假設應力方向一致。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Align old-bore movement with new-face distance while excluding thermal drift. Compare in-situ stress measurements, rock tests and wall-damage orientation, then use multipoint extensometers to test consistency with the assumed stress directions. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「洞壁切向應力」的交付需回答：把原孔位移與新掌子面距離對齊，排除溫度漂移。保留應力模型的座標、邊界和材料假設，量測與預測不符時先核對代表性，再由岩力設計者選擇非線性或節理模型。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Frejus Road Tunnel, the tangential wall stress handover must address the following evidence: Align old-bore movement with new-face distance while excluding thermal drift. Record stress-model coordinates, boundaries and material assumptions; when observations disagree, check representativeness before the rock designer selects nonlinear or jointed models.","failure":"注意干擾：未扣溫度的位移可能被誤判成新孔造成的地盤作用。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Uncorrected thermal movement can be misattributed to excavation interaction. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b115-v14-11-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"把原孔位移與新掌子面距離對齊，排除溫度漂移。將原位應力量測、岩石試驗及洞壁破壞方位相互比較，再用多點伸長計檢查變形是否與所假設應力方向一致。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Align old-bore movement with new-face distance while excluding thermal drift. Compare in-situ stress measurements, rock tests and wall-damage orientation, then use multipoint extensometers to test consistency with the assumed stress directions. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b115-v14-11-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「洞壁切向應力」的交付需回答：把原孔位移與新掌子面距離對齊，排除溫度漂移。保留應力模型的座標、邊界和材料假設，量測與預測不符時先核對代表性，再由岩力設計者選擇非線性或節理模型。","textEn":"For Frejus Road Tunnel, the tangential wall stress handover must address the following evidence: Align old-bore movement with new-face distance while excluding thermal drift. Record stress-model coordinates, boundaries and material assumptions; when observations disagree, check representativeness before the rock designer selects nonlinear or jointed models.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「覆土應力與洞壁重分配」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Cover stress and wall redistribution\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","全部檔案上傳完成就代表工程交接已經驗收合格。","把原孔位移與新掌子面距離對齊，排除溫度漂移。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","Uploading all files means that engineering handover has been accepted.","Align old-bore movement with new-face distance while excluding thermal drift."],"answer":2,"explanation":"把原孔位移與新掌子面距離對齊，排除溫度漂移。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Align old-bore movement with new-face distance while excluding thermal drift. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":11},{"id":"b115-v14-12","title":"覆土應力與洞壁重分配：失效診斷","titleEn":"Cover stress and wall redistribution: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b115-v14-11"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「洞壁切向應力」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Tangential wall stress” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"未扣溫度的位移可能被誤判成新孔造成的地盤作用。把彈性峰值直接當岩體強度可能誤判支護需求；相反地忽略剝落或擠壓也會讓局部破壞逐步侵入淨空。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Uncorrected thermal movement can be misattributed to excavation interaction. Equating an elastic peak with rock-mass strength misjudges support demand; overlooking spalling or squeezing lets damage progressively consume clearance. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：圓孔彈性解可辨識量級，但節理、非圓斷面、塑性區與原位應力比會改變峰值位置，不能只用覆土重量推定全部三維應力。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Cover weight alone cannot establish the complete three-dimensional stress state or support demand.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「知道覆土深度就能唯一決定洞壁各方向的應力。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Cover depth uniquely determines wall stress in every direction.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b115-v14-12-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"未扣溫度的位移可能被誤判成新孔造成的地盤作用。把彈性峰值直接當岩體強度可能誤判支護需求；相反地忽略剝落或擠壓也會讓局部破壞逐步侵入淨空。","textEn":"Uncorrected thermal movement can be misattributed to excavation interaction. Equating an elastic peak with rock-mass strength misjudges support demand; overlooking spalling or squeezing lets damage progressively consume clearance.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b115-v14-12-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「覆土應力與洞壁重分配」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Cover stress and wall redistribution\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["未扣溫度的位移可能被誤判成新孔造成的地盤作用。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","支護越厚越硬就一定能解決所有擠壓性地層。"],"optionsEn":["Uncorrected thermal movement can be misattributed to excavation interaction.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","Thicker and stiffer support necessarily solves every squeezing-ground problem."],"answer":0,"explanation":"未扣溫度的位移可能被誤判成新孔造成的地盤作用。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Uncorrected thermal movement can be misattributed to excavation interaction. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":12},{"id":"b115-v14-13","title":"支護啟動與變形容量：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Support activation and deformation capacity: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b115-v14-12"],"objective":"說明「支護安裝時點」如何影響弗雷瑞斯公路隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Support activation time” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Frejus Road Tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"弗雷瑞斯新舊支護設計背景不同，教材比較荷載啟動時點及長期劣化，不只比較材料強度。支護荷載由開挖釋放量和支護啟動時間共同決定，越早安裝不一定讓構件受力越小。地盤反力與支護曲線必須連同掌子面距離及封閉順序理解；擠壓性地層還需保留變形容量，不能只追求高剛度與高材料強度。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「支護安裝時點」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"New and old support have different histories; compare activation time and ageing rather than material strength alone. Support load depends on stress release and activation time, so earlier installation does not necessarily reduce member forces. Interpret ground-reaction and support curves together with distance from the face and closure sequence. Squeezing ground also needs deformation capacity; high stiffness and material strength alone do not guarantee a compatible support response. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Support activation time” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：局部剛度=44 kN/mm；位移=8 mm。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: local stiffness=44 kN/mm; movement=8 mm.","failure":"常見誤解：「支護越厚越硬就一定能解決所有擠壓性地層。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Thicker and stiffer support necessarily solves every squeezing-ground problem.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「支護安裝時點」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Support activation time”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b115-v14-13-k1","title":"支護啟動與變形容量","titleEn":"Support activation and deformation capacity","text":"弗雷瑞斯新舊支護設計背景不同，教材比較荷載啟動時點及長期劣化，不只比較材料強度。支護荷載由開挖釋放量和支護啟動時間共同決定，越早安裝不一定讓構件受力越小。","textEn":"New and old support have different histories; compare activation time and ageing rather than material strength alone. Support load depends on stress release and activation time, so earlier installation does not necessarily reduce member forces.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b115-v14-13-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：支護越厚越硬就一定能解決所有擠壓性地層。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Thicker and stiffer support necessarily solves every squeezing-ground problem. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「支護啟動與變形容量」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Support activation and deformation capacity\" is correct?","options":["支護越厚越硬就一定能解決所有擠壓性地層。","弗雷瑞斯新舊支護設計背景不同，教材比較荷載啟動時點及長期劣化，不只比較材料強度。","混凝土強度達標就不必檢查接縫轉動與偏壓。"],"optionsEn":["Thicker and stiffer support necessarily solves every squeezing-ground problem.","New and old support have different histories; compare activation time and ageing rather than material strength alone.","Passing concrete strength eliminates the need to check joint rotation and uneven pressure."],"answer":1,"explanation":"弗雷瑞斯新舊支護設計背景不同，教材比較荷載啟動時點及長期劣化，不只比較材料強度。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"New and old support have different histories; compare activation time and ageing rather than material strength alone. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":13},{"id":"b115-v14-14","title":"支護啟動與變形容量：定量估算","titleEn":"Support activation and deformation capacity: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b115-v14-13"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「支護安裝時點」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Support activation time” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：局部剛度=44 kN/mm；位移=8 mm。F=ku=352 kN。僅把位移增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為387.2 kN。邊界：線性局部彈簧，不含屈服或時間效應；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: local stiffness=44 kN/mm; movement=8 mm. F=ku=352 kN. Increasing only movement by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 387.2 kN. Boundary: Local linear spring without yielding or time effects. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：分別建立新支護荷重與舊支護檢查的時間基準。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Maintain separate time references for new support loads and legacy inspections.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b115-v14-14-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：局部剛度=44 kN/mm；位移=8 mm。F=ku=352 kN。僅把位移增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為387.2 kN。邊界：線性局部彈簧，不含屈服或時間效應；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: local stiffness=44 kN/mm; movement=8 mm. F=ku=352 kN. Increasing only movement by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 387.2 kN. Boundary: Local linear spring without yielding or time effects. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b115-v14-14-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「支護啟動與變形容量」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Support activation and deformation capacity\", which statement holds?","options":["照度越高就必然使隧道內所有物體更容易辨識。","設備有兩台就可以直接把各自故障率相乘判定安全。","原創教學假設：局部剛度=44 kN/mm；位移=8 mm。"],"optionsEn":["Higher illuminance necessarily makes every tunnel object easier to detect.","Two units allow their failure probabilities to be multiplied directly to establish safety.","Original teaching assumptions: local stiffness=44 kN/mm; movement=8 mm."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設：局部剛度=44 kN/mm；位移=8 mm。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: local stiffness=44 kN/mm; movement=8 mm. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":14},{"id":"b115-v14-15","title":"支護啟動與變形容量：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Support activation and deformation capacity: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b115-v14-14"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「支護安裝時點」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Support activation time” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"分別建立新支護荷重與舊支護檢查的時間基準。同步記錄收斂、支護荷重與安裝里程，比較同一地質分區內的速率及荷載，不將不同開挖齡期讀值直接混合。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Maintain separate time references for new support loads and legacy inspections. Synchronise convergence, support loads and installation chainage; compare rates and loads within one ground domain without mixing readings at different excavation ages. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「支護安裝時點」的交付需回答：分別建立新支護荷重與舊支護檢查的時間基準。把安裝時間和量測資料一起交付支護設計者，任何級別變更都需地質及位移證據，不能憑單一瞬間讀值自行改支護。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Frejus Road Tunnel, the support activation time handover must address the following evidence: Maintain separate time references for new support loads and legacy inspections. Submit installation times with measurements to the support designer; class changes need both ground and movement evidence, not an isolated instantaneous reading.","failure":"注意干擾：新支護較強不能證明舊孔整修可省略施工階段分析。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Stronger new support does not remove staging analysis for old-bore refurbishment. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b115-v14-15-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"分別建立新支護荷重與舊支護檢查的時間基準。同步記錄收斂、支護荷重與安裝里程，比較同一地質分區內的速率及荷載，不將不同開挖齡期讀值直接混合。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Maintain separate time references for new support loads and legacy inspections. Synchronise convergence, support loads and installation chainage; compare rates and loads within one ground domain without mixing readings at different excavation ages. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b115-v14-15-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「支護安裝時點」的交付需回答：分別建立新支護荷重與舊支護檢查的時間基準。把安裝時間和量測資料一起交付支護設計者，任何級別變更都需地質及位移證據，不能憑單一瞬間讀值自行改支護。","textEn":"For Frejus Road Tunnel, the support activation time handover must address the following evidence: Maintain separate time references for new support loads and legacy inspections. Submit installation times with measurements to the support designer; class changes need both ground and movement evidence, not an isolated instantaneous reading.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「支護啟動與變形容量」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Support activation and deformation capacity\"?","options":["分別建立新支護荷重與舊支護檢查的時間基準。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","最短的隧道路線一定也有最低施工與維護風險。"],"optionsEn":["Maintain separate time references for new support loads and legacy inspections.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","The shortest tunnel alignment necessarily has the lowest construction and maintenance risk."],"answer":0,"explanation":"分別建立新支護荷重與舊支護檢查的時間基準。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Maintain separate time references for new support loads and legacy inspections. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":15},{"id":"b115-v14-16","title":"支護啟動與變形容量：失效診斷","titleEn":"Support activation and deformation capacity: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b115-v14-15"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「支護安裝時點」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Support activation time” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"新支護較強不能證明舊孔整修可省略施工階段分析。過晚封閉會讓不可回復變形增加，過硬且行程不足的支護也可能脆裂，兩者都可能表現為裂縫而需不同處理。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Stronger new support does not remove staging analysis for old-bore refurbishment. Late closure increases irreversible movement, while excessively stiff support with little travel can fail brittly; both produce cracks but require different diagnoses. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：地盤反力與支護曲線必須連同掌子面距離及封閉順序理解；擠壓性地層還需保留變形容量，不能只追求高剛度與高材料強度。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Squeezing ground also needs deformation capacity; high stiffness and material strength alone do not guarantee a compatible support response.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「支護越厚越硬就一定能解決所有擠壓性地層。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Thicker and stiffer support necessarily solves every squeezing-ground problem.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b115-v14-16-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"新支護較強不能證明舊孔整修可省略施工階段分析。過晚封閉會讓不可回復變形增加，過硬且行程不足的支護也可能脆裂，兩者都可能表現為裂縫而需不同處理。","textEn":"Stronger new support does not remove staging analysis for old-bore refurbishment. Late closure increases irreversible movement, while excessively stiff support with little travel can fail brittly; both produce cracks but require different diagnoses.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b115-v14-16-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「支護啟動與變形容量」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Support activation and deformation capacity\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","新支護較強不能證明舊孔整修可省略施工階段分析。","混凝土強度達標就不必檢查接縫轉動與偏壓。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Stronger new support does not remove staging analysis for old-bore refurbishment.","Passing concrete strength eliminates the need to check joint rotation and uneven pressure."],"answer":1,"explanation":"新支護較強不能證明舊孔整修可省略施工階段分析。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Stronger new support does not remove staging analysis for old-bore refurbishment. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":16}],"order":2},{"id":"b115-v14-s3","title":"施工方法與施工階段控制","titleEn":"Construction methods and stage control","description":"本階段聚焦「環向受力與接縫柔度」與「通風網路與壓力損失」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Ring force and joint flexibility\" and \"Ventilation network and pressure loss\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b115-v14-17","title":"環向受力與接縫柔度：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Ring force and joint flexibility: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b115-v14-16"],"objective":"說明「襯砌環向壓縮」如何影響弗雷瑞斯公路隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Lining hoop compression” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Frejus Road Tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"重車公路的襯砌和設備支承有不同作用，教材用均勻外壓示例後再辨識附掛設備局部荷載。圓形襯砌對均勻外壓可主要以環向壓縮抵抗，但接頭轉動、偏壓與背填空隙會引起彎矩。薄環膜應力只說明其中一條受力路徑；脫模、運輸、頂推及永久狀態的荷載不同，環片局部接觸與止水條件必須另外檢核。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「襯砌環向壓縮」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Lining and equipment supports carry different actions; follow a uniform-pressure example with identification of local suspended loads. A circular lining resists uniform external pressure largely through hoop compression, but joint rotation, uneven load and backfill voids generate bending. Thin-ring membrane stress describes only one load path. Demoulding, transport, jacking and permanent states impose different actions, requiring separate checks of local segment contact and sealing rather than one permanent-load calculation. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Lining hoop compression” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：均勻外壓=0.58 MPa；半徑=3.4 m；厚度=0.35 m。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: uniform external pressure=0.58 MPa; radius=3.4 m; thickness=0.35 m. σθ=pr/t=5.63429 MPa.","failure":"常見誤解：「混凝土強度達標就不必檢查接縫轉動與偏壓。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Passing concrete strength eliminates the need to check joint rotation and uneven pressure.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「襯砌環向壓縮」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Lining hoop compression”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b115-v14-17-k1","title":"環向受力與接縫柔度","titleEn":"Ring force and joint flexibility","text":"重車公路的襯砌和設備支承有不同作用，教材用均勻外壓示例後再辨識附掛設備局部荷載。圓形襯砌對均勻外壓可主要以環向壓縮抵抗，但接頭轉動、偏壓與背填空隙會引起彎矩。","textEn":"Lining and equipment supports carry different actions; follow a uniform-pressure example with identification of local suspended loads. A circular lining resists uniform external pressure largely through hoop compression, but joint rotation, uneven load and backfill voids generate bending.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b115-v14-17-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：混凝土強度達標就不必檢查接縫轉動與偏壓。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Passing concrete strength eliminates the need to check joint rotation and uneven pressure. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「環向受力與接縫柔度」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Ring force and joint flexibility\" is correct?","options":["混凝土強度達標就不必檢查接縫轉動與偏壓。","風機銘牌風量相加就是全隧道各處可用的通風量。","重車公路的襯砌和設備支承有不同作用，教材用均勻外壓示例後再辨識附掛設備局部荷載。"],"optionsEn":["Passing concrete strength eliminates the need to check joint rotation and uneven pressure.","Adding fan nameplate flows gives the usable airflow everywhere in the tunnel.","Lining and equipment supports carry different actions; follow a uniform-pressure example with identification of local suspended loads."],"answer":2,"explanation":"重車公路的襯砌和設備支承有不同作用，教材用均勻外壓示例後再辨識附掛設備局部荷載。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Lining and equipment supports carry different actions; follow a uniform-pressure example with identification of local suspended loads. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":17},{"id":"b115-v14-18","title":"環向受力與接縫柔度：定量估算","titleEn":"Ring force and joint flexibility: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b115-v14-17"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「襯砌環向壓縮」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Lining hoop compression” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：均勻外壓=0.58 MPa；半徑=3.4 m；厚度=0.35 m。σθ=pr/t=5.63429 MPa。僅把均勻外壓增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為6.19771 MPa。邊界：薄圓環膜應力，不是接縫、偏壓或矩形框架解；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: uniform external pressure=0.58 MPa; radius=3.4 m; thickness=0.35 m. σθ=pr/t=5.63429 MPa. Increasing only uniform external pressure by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 6.19771 MPa. Boundary: Thin circular-ring membrane stress, not a joint, uneven-load or rectangular-frame solution. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：核對設備錨固位置、裂縫圖及襯砌實際厚度。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Check equipment anchorage, crack maps and actual lining thickness.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b115-v14-18-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：均勻外壓=0.58 MPa；半徑=3.4 m；厚度=0.35 m。σθ=pr/t=5.63429 MPa。僅把均勻外壓增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為6.19771 MPa。邊界：薄圓環膜應力，不是接縫、偏壓或矩形框架解；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: uniform external pressure=0.58 MPa; radius=3.4 m; thickness=0.35 m. σθ=pr/t=5.63429 MPa. Increasing only uniform external pressure by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 6.19771 MPa. Boundary: Thin circular-ring membrane stress, not a joint, uneven-load or rectangular-frame solution. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b115-v14-18-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「環向受力與接縫柔度」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Ring force and joint flexibility\", which statement holds?","options":["原創教學假設：均勻外壓=0.58 MPa；半徑=3.4 m；厚度=0.35 m。","只要出口距離短，就不需要比較可用與所需安全時間。","全部檔案上傳完成就代表工程交接已經驗收合格。"],"optionsEn":["Original teaching assumptions: uniform external pressure=0.58 MPa; radius=3.4 m; thickness=0.35 m. σθ=pr/t=5.63429 MPa.","Short exit distance removes the need to compare available and required safe time.","Uploading all files means that engineering handover has been accepted."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創教學假設：均勻外壓=0.58 MPa；半徑=3.4 m；厚度=0.35 m。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: uniform external pressure=0.58 MPa; radius=3.4 m; thickness=0.35 m. σθ=pr/t=5.63429 MPa. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":18},{"id":"b115-v14-19","title":"環向受力與接縫柔度：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Ring force and joint flexibility: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b115-v14-18"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「襯砌環向壓縮」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Lining hoop compression” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"核對設備錨固位置、裂縫圖及襯砌實際厚度。將環形變形、接縫張開與應變和含接頭彈簧的模型比較，分開安裝後、背填後及水頭回升後的基準。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Check equipment anchorage, crack maps and actual lining thickness. Compare ring distortion, joint opening and strain with a joint-spring model, separating baselines after installation, grouting and head recovery. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「襯砌環向壓縮」的交付需回答：核對設備錨固位置、裂縫圖及襯砌實際厚度。設計圖應分開標註各施工階段、接頭剛度及背填條件，構件驗收同時核對幾何、材料批次與止水試驗適用包絡。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Frejus Road Tunnel, the lining hoop compression handover must address the following evidence: Check equipment anchorage, crack maps and actual lining thickness. Drawings distinguish stages, joint stiffness and backfill conditions; component acceptance reconciles geometry, material batches and the applicable sealing-test envelope.","failure":"注意干擾：新增設備未回查襯砌狀態可能把局部負擔集中在弱區。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: New equipment without lining-condition checks can concentrate load in weak zones. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b115-v14-19-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"核對設備錨固位置、裂縫圖及襯砌實際厚度。將環形變形、接縫張開與應變和含接頭彈簧的模型比較，分開安裝後、背填後及水頭回升後的基準。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Check equipment anchorage, crack maps and actual lining thickness. Compare ring distortion, joint opening and strain with a joint-spring model, separating baselines after installation, grouting and head recovery. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b115-v14-19-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「襯砌環向壓縮」的交付需回答：核對設備錨固位置、裂縫圖及襯砌實際厚度。設計圖應分開標註各施工階段、接頭剛度及背填條件，構件驗收同時核對幾何、材料批次與止水試驗適用包絡。","textEn":"For Frejus Road Tunnel, the lining hoop compression handover must address the following evidence: Check equipment anchorage, crack maps and actual lining thickness. Drawings distinguish stages, joint stiffness and backfill conditions; component acceptance reconciles geometry, material batches and the applicable sealing-test envelope.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「環向受力與接縫柔度」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Ring force and joint flexibility\"?","options":["允收準則可以等看到量測數據後再決定。","核對設備錨固位置、裂縫圖及襯砌實際厚度。","岩芯很硬就可以排除破碎帶變形與集中湧水。"],"optionsEn":["Acceptance criteria can be decided after the measured data have been seen.","Check equipment anchorage, crack maps and actual lining thickness.","Hard intact core excludes fault-zone deformation and concentrated inflow."],"answer":1,"explanation":"核對設備錨固位置、裂縫圖及襯砌實際厚度。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Check equipment anchorage, crack maps and actual lining thickness. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":19},{"id":"b115-v14-20","title":"環向受力與接縫柔度：失效診斷","titleEn":"Ring force and joint flexibility: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b115-v14-19"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「襯砌環向壓縮」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Lining hoop compression” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"新增設備未回查襯砌狀態可能把局部負擔集中在弱區。局部脫空增加環片彎曲，裂縫未必代表混凝土平均強度不足；忽略接縫接觸會把補強方向導向錯誤位置。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"New equipment without lining-condition checks can concentrate load in weak zones. Local voids increase bending, so cracks need not indicate inadequate mean concrete strength; neglecting joint contact can misdirect strengthening. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：薄環膜應力只說明其中一條受力路徑；脫模、運輸、頂推及永久狀態的荷載不同，環片局部接觸與止水條件必須另外檢核。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Demoulding, transport, jacking and permanent states impose different actions, requiring separate checks of local segment contact and sealing rather than one permanent-load calculation.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「混凝土強度達標就不必檢查接縫轉動與偏壓。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Passing concrete strength eliminates the need to check joint rotation and uneven pressure.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b115-v14-20-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"新增設備未回查襯砌狀態可能把局部負擔集中在弱區。局部脫空增加環片彎曲，裂縫未必代表混凝土平均強度不足；忽略接縫接觸會把補強方向導向錯誤位置。","textEn":"New equipment without lining-condition checks can concentrate load in weak zones. Local voids increase bending, so cracks need not indicate inadequate mean concrete strength; neglecting joint contact can misdirect strengthening.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b115-v14-20-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「環向受力與接縫柔度」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Ring force and joint flexibility\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["症狀相同就代表原因相同，不必用量測區分。","風機銘牌風量相加就是全隧道各處可用的通風量。","新增設備未回查襯砌狀態可能把局部負擔集中在弱區。"],"optionsEn":["Identical symptoms always mean identical causes, so no discriminating measurement is needed.","Adding fan nameplate flows gives the usable airflow everywhere in the tunnel.","New equipment without lining-condition checks can concentrate load in weak zones."],"answer":2,"explanation":"新增設備未回查襯砌狀態可能把局部負擔集中在弱區。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"New equipment without lining-condition checks can concentrate load in weak zones. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":20},{"id":"b115-v14-21","title":"通風網路與壓力損失：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Ventilation network and pressure loss: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b115-v14-20"],"objective":"說明「風道摩擦壓損」如何影響弗雷瑞斯公路隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Duct friction loss” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Frejus Road Tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"分向孔與原雙向情境的車流助風不同，弗雷瑞斯教材要求換孔後重新核對通風邊界。風機提供壓差，實際風量由風道摩阻、局部損失、外風與其他風機共同決定。支路開關會重新分配整個網路，不能把額定風量直接加總；正常污染稀釋與火災控煙也有不同目標，需要分別建立受控邊界和故障情境。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「風道摩擦壓損」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Directional tubes differ from former bidirectional traffic in piston effects; recheck airflow boundaries after configuration changes. Fans supply pressure, but actual flow follows friction, local losses, external wind and interactions with other fans. Switching a branch redistributes the network rather than simply adding rated flows. Routine dilution and fire smoke control have different objectives, so each needs explicit boundaries, operating states and failure cases rather than one universal flow target. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Duct friction loss” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：達西因子=0.025 無因次；風道長度=1060 m；水力直徑=4 m；空氣密度=1.2 kg/m³；平均風速=3.5 m/s。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: Darcy factor=0.025 dimensionless; duct length=1060 m; hydraulic diameter=4 m; air density=1.2 kg/m³; mean velocity=3.5 m/s. Δp=f(L/D)ρv²/2=48.6937 Pa.","failure":"常見誤解：「風機銘牌風量相加就是全隧道各處可用的通風量。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Adding fan nameplate flows gives the usable airflow everywhere in the tunnel.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「風道摩擦壓損」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Duct friction loss”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b115-v14-21-k1","title":"通風網路與壓力損失","titleEn":"Ventilation network and pressure loss","text":"分向孔與原雙向情境的車流助風不同，弗雷瑞斯教材要求換孔後重新核對通風邊界。風機提供壓差，實際風量由風道摩阻、局部損失、外風與其他風機共同決定。","textEn":"Directional tubes differ from former bidirectional traffic in piston effects; recheck airflow boundaries after configuration changes. Fans supply pressure, but actual flow follows friction, local losses, external wind and interactions with other fans.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b115-v14-21-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：風機銘牌風量相加就是全隧道各處可用的通風量。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Adding fan nameplate flows gives the usable airflow everywhere in the tunnel. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「通風網路與壓力損失」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Ventilation network and pressure loss\" is correct?","options":["分向孔與原雙向情境的車流助風不同，弗雷瑞斯教材要求換孔後重新核對通風邊界。","風機銘牌風量相加就是全隧道各處可用的通風量。","照度越高就必然使隧道內所有物體更容易辨識。"],"optionsEn":["Directional tubes differ from former bidirectional traffic in piston effects; recheck airflow boundaries after configuration changes.","Adding fan nameplate flows gives the usable airflow everywhere in the tunnel.","Higher illuminance necessarily makes every tunnel object easier to detect."],"answer":0,"explanation":"分向孔與原雙向情境的車流助風不同，弗雷瑞斯教材要求換孔後重新核對通風邊界。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Directional tubes differ from former bidirectional traffic in piston effects; recheck airflow boundaries after configuration changes. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":21},{"id":"b115-v14-22","title":"通風網路與壓力損失：定量估算","titleEn":"Ventilation network and pressure loss: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b115-v14-21"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「風道摩擦壓損」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Duct friction loss” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：達西因子=0.025 無因次；風道長度=1060 m；水力直徑=4 m；空氣密度=1.2 kg/m³；平均風速=3.5 m/s。Δp=f(L/D)ρv²/2=48.6937 Pa。僅把平均風速增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為58.9194 Pa。邊界：定密度直管摩阻，局部損失及外風另計；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: Darcy factor=0.025 dimensionless; duct length=1060 m; hydraulic diameter=4 m; air density=1.2 kg/m³; mean velocity=3.5 m/s. Δp=f(L/D)ρv²/2=48.6937 Pa. Increasing only mean velocity by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 58.9194 Pa. Boundary: Constant-density straight-duct friction; local loss and external wind are separate. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：對比切換前後同風機設定的實測壓差和流量。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Compare measured pressure and flow at equal fan settings before and after transfer.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b115-v14-22-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：達西因子=0.025 無因次；風道長度=1060 m；水力直徑=4 m；空氣密度=1.2 kg/m³；平均風速=3.5 m/s。Δp=f(L/D)ρv²/2=48.6937 Pa。僅把平均風速增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為58.9194 Pa。邊界：定密度直管摩阻，局部損失及外風另計；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: Darcy factor=0.025 dimensionless; duct length=1060 m; hydraulic diameter=4 m; air density=1.2 kg/m³; mean velocity=3.5 m/s. Δp=f(L/D)ρv²/2=48.6937 Pa. Increasing only mean velocity by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 58.9194 Pa. Boundary: Constant-density straight-duct friction; local loss and external wind are separate. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b115-v14-22-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「通風網路與壓力損失」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Ventilation network and pressure loss\", which statement holds?","options":["設備有兩台就可以直接把各自故障率相乘判定安全。","原創教學假設：達西因子=0.025 無因次；風道長度=1060 m；水力直徑=4 m；空氣密度=1.2 kg/m³；平均風速=3.5 m/s。","最短的隧道路線一定也有最低施工與維護風險。"],"optionsEn":["Two units allow their failure probabilities to be multiplied directly to establish safety.","Original teaching assumptions: Darcy factor=0.025 dimensionless.","The shortest tunnel alignment necessarily has the lowest construction and maintenance risk."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創教學假設：達西因子=0.025 無因次；風道長度=1060 m；水力直徑=4 m；空氣密度=1.2 kg/m³；平均風速=3.5 m/s。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: Darcy factor=0.025 dimensionless; duct length=1060 m; hydraulic diameter=4 m; air density=1.2 kg/m³; mean velocity=3.5 m/s. Δp=f(L/D)ρv²/2=48.6937 Pa. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":22},{"id":"b115-v14-23","title":"通風網路與壓力損失：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Ventilation network and pressure loss: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b115-v14-22"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「風道摩擦壓損」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Duct friction loss” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"對比切換前後同風機設定的實測壓差和流量。沿線同步量測靜壓與風速，記錄風門及其他風機狀態，再把實測工作點和風機曲線、網路壓損比較。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Compare measured pressure and flow at equal fan settings before and after transfer. Measure pressure and velocity synchronously, record dampers and other fans, and compare the measured duty point with fan curves and network resistance. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「風道摩擦壓損」的交付需回答：對比切換前後同風機設定的實測壓差和流量。驗收採明確風門和車流邊界，維修改線後重新核對網路工作點，火災模式由防災責任工程師簽認而非沿用正常模式。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Frejus Road Tunnel, the duct friction loss handover must address the following evidence: Compare measured pressure and flow at equal fan settings before and after transfer. Commission with specified damper and traffic boundaries, recheck duty points after rerouting, and have the fire-safety engineer approve emergency modes independently.","failure":"注意干擾：沿用舊控制參數可能在新車流方向下產生不符預期風向。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Old controls may produce unintended airflow under the new traffic direction. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b115-v14-23-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"對比切換前後同風機設定的實測壓差和流量。沿線同步量測靜壓與風速，記錄風門及其他風機狀態，再把實測工作點和風機曲線、網路壓損比較。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Compare measured pressure and flow at equal fan settings before and after transfer. Measure pressure and velocity synchronously, record dampers and other fans, and compare the measured duty point with fan curves and network resistance. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b115-v14-23-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「風道摩擦壓損」的交付需回答：對比切換前後同風機設定的實測壓差和流量。驗收採明確風門和車流邊界，維修改線後重新核對網路工作點，火災模式由防災責任工程師簽認而非沿用正常模式。","textEn":"For Frejus Road Tunnel, the duct friction loss handover must address the following evidence: Compare measured pressure and flow at equal fan settings before and after transfer. Commission with specified damper and traffic boundaries, recheck duty points after rerouting, and have the fire-safety engineer approve emergency modes independently.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「通風網路與壓力損失」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Ventilation network and pressure loss\"?","options":["只要結構分析模型看起來合理，就可以省略現場量測與試驗。","知道覆土深度就能唯一決定洞壁各方向的應力。","對比切換前後同風機設定的實測壓差和流量。"],"optionsEn":["If the structural model looks reasonable, site measurement and testing can be skipped.","Cover depth uniquely determines wall stress in every direction.","Compare measured pressure and flow at equal fan settings before and after transfer."],"answer":2,"explanation":"對比切換前後同風機設定的實測壓差和流量。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Compare measured pressure and flow at equal fan settings before and after transfer. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":23},{"id":"b115-v14-24","title":"通風網路與壓力損失：失效診斷","titleEn":"Ventilation network and pressure loss: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b115-v14-23"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「風道摩擦壓損」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Duct friction loss” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"沿用舊控制參數可能在新車流方向下產生不符預期風向。只看風機轉速會漏掉風門誤位或短路漏風，可能在總耗電增加時，真正需要的區段反而風量不足。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Old controls may produce unintended airflow under the new traffic direction. Fan speed alone misses a misplaced damper or leakage shortcut; total power may rise while the critical section receives less air. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：支路開關會重新分配整個網路，不能把額定風量直接加總；正常污染稀釋與火災控煙也有不同目標，需要分別建立受控邊界和故障情境。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Routine dilution and fire smoke control have different objectives, so each needs explicit boundaries, operating states and failure cases rather than one universal flow target.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「風機銘牌風量相加就是全隧道各處可用的通風量。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Adding fan nameplate flows gives the usable airflow everywhere in the tunnel.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b115-v14-24-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"沿用舊控制參數可能在新車流方向下產生不符預期風向。只看風機轉速會漏掉風門誤位或短路漏風，可能在總耗電增加時，真正需要的區段反而風量不足。","textEn":"Old controls may produce unintended airflow under the new traffic direction. Fan speed alone misses a misplaced damper or leakage shortcut; total power may rise while the critical section receives less air.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b115-v14-24-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「通風網路與壓力損失」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Ventilation network and pressure loss\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["沿用舊控制參數可能在新車流方向下產生不符預期風向。","只要結構還沒倒，就代表安全餘裕仍然足夠。","照度越高就必然使隧道內所有物體更容易辨識。"],"optionsEn":["Old controls may produce unintended airflow under the new traffic direction.","As long as the structure is still standing, its safety margin must still be adequate.","Higher illuminance necessarily makes every tunnel object easier to detect."],"answer":0,"explanation":"沿用舊控制參數可能在新車流方向下產生不符預期風向。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Old controls may produce unintended airflow under the new traffic direction. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":24}],"order":3},{"id":"b115-v14-s4","title":"試驗、量測與監測驗證","titleEn":"Testing, measurement and monitoring","description":"本階段聚焦「視覺適應與路面亮度」與「疏散時間與分區可用性」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Visual adaptation and pavement luminance\" and \"Evacuation time and zone availability\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b115-v14-25","title":"視覺適應與路面亮度：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Visual adaptation and pavement luminance: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b115-v14-24"],"objective":"說明「漫反射亮度」如何影響弗雷瑞斯公路隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Diffuse luminance” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Frejus Road Tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"新舊孔表面與燈具狀態不同，教學比較相同照度下路面反射造成的亮度差。駕駛從洞外進入洞內時視覺適應需要時間，照度並不等同從駕駛視角看到的亮度。路面反射、濕度、燈具配光及背景對比共同影響辨識；朗伯模型只示範理想漫反射，不能直接制定入口段燈具間距或真實道路安全值。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「漫反射亮度」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Different surfaces and luminaires in old and new tubes can produce different luminance at equal illuminance. Driver adaptation takes time when entering a tunnel, and illuminance is not the luminance seen from the driving position. Pavement reflection, wetness, luminaire distribution and background contrast affect detection. A Lambertian model illustrates ideal diffuse reflection only; it cannot establish entrance-zone spacing or actual road-safety limits without photometric and operational assessment. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Diffuse luminance” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：照度=108 lx；反射率=0.26 無因次。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: illuminance=108 lx; reflectance=0.26 dimensionless.","failure":"常見誤解：「照度越高就必然使隧道內所有物體更容易辨識。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Higher illuminance necessarily makes every tunnel object easier to detect.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「漫反射亮度」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Diffuse luminance”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b115-v14-25-k1","title":"視覺適應與路面亮度","titleEn":"Visual adaptation and pavement luminance","text":"新舊孔表面與燈具狀態不同，教學比較相同照度下路面反射造成的亮度差。駕駛從洞外進入洞內時視覺適應需要時間，照度並不等同從駕駛視角看到的亮度。","textEn":"Different surfaces and luminaires in old and new tubes can produce different luminance at equal illuminance. Driver adaptation takes time when entering a tunnel, and illuminance is not the luminance seen from the driving position.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b115-v14-25-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：照度越高就必然使隧道內所有物體更容易辨識。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Higher illuminance necessarily makes every tunnel object easier to detect. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「視覺適應與路面亮度」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Visual adaptation and pavement luminance\" is correct?","options":["照度越高就必然使隧道內所有物體更容易辨識。","新舊孔表面與燈具狀態不同，教學比較相同照度下路面反射造成的亮度差。","只要出口距離短，就不需要比較可用與所需安全時間。"],"optionsEn":["Higher illuminance necessarily makes every tunnel object easier to detect.","Different surfaces and luminaires in old and new tubes can produce different luminance at equal illuminance.","Short exit distance removes the need to compare available and required safe time."],"answer":1,"explanation":"新舊孔表面與燈具狀態不同，教學比較相同照度下路面反射造成的亮度差。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Different surfaces and luminaires in old and new tubes can produce different luminance at equal illuminance. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":25},{"id":"b115-v14-26","title":"視覺適應與路面亮度：定量估算","titleEn":"Visual adaptation and pavement luminance: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b115-v14-25"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「漫反射亮度」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Diffuse luminance” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：照度=108 lx；反射率=0.26 無因次。L=ρE/π=8.93814 cd/m²。僅把照度增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為9.83196 cd/m²。邊界：理想朗伯漫反射，不是真實濕路面亮度；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: illuminance=108 lx; reflectance=0.26 dimensionless. L=ρE/π=8.93814 cd/m². Increasing only illuminance by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 9.83196 cd/m². Boundary: Ideal Lambertian reflection, not actual wet-road luminance. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以同視角和乾濕條件比較兩孔的光度量測。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Compare photometry in both tubes under equal viewing and wetness conditions.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b115-v14-26-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：照度=108 lx；反射率=0.26 無因次。L=ρE/π=8.93814 cd/m²。僅把照度增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為9.83196 cd/m²。邊界：理想朗伯漫反射，不是真實濕路面亮度；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: illuminance=108 lx; reflectance=0.26 dimensionless. L=ρE/π=8.93814 cd/m². Increasing only illuminance by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 9.83196 cd/m². Boundary: Ideal Lambertian reflection, not actual wet-road luminance. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b115-v14-26-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「視覺適應與路面亮度」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Visual adaptation and pavement luminance\", which statement holds?","options":["全部檔案上傳完成就代表工程交接已經驗收合格。","岩芯很硬就可以排除破碎帶變形與集中湧水。","原創教學假設：照度=108 lx；反射率=0.26 無因次。"],"optionsEn":["Uploading all files means that engineering handover has been accepted.","Hard intact core excludes fault-zone deformation and concentrated inflow.","Original teaching assumptions: illuminance=108 lx; reflectance=0.26 dimensionless."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設：照度=108 lx；反射率=0.26 無因次。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: illuminance=108 lx; reflectance=0.26 dimensionless. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":26},{"id":"b115-v14-27","title":"視覺適應與路面亮度：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Visual adaptation and pavement luminance: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b115-v14-26"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「漫反射亮度」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Diffuse luminance” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以同視角和乾濕條件比較兩孔的光度量測。以駕駛視角的亮度量測配合照度網格，分別檢查乾濕路面與燈具衰減，保留外部天空條件。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Compare photometry in both tubes under equal viewing and wetness conditions. Combine driver-view luminance with illuminance grids, checking dry and wet pavement and lamp depreciation while preserving exterior sky conditions. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「漫反射亮度」的交付需回答：以同視角和乾濕條件比較兩孔的光度量測。將視角、路面狀態和光度校正連同量測交付，照明調整需按核准場景測試，不把理想反射公式當驗收標準。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Frejus Road Tunnel, the diffuse luminance handover must address the following evidence: Compare photometry in both tubes under equal viewing and wetness conditions. Hand over viewing geometry, pavement state and photometric calibration; test changes against approved scenarios rather than treating ideal reflection as an acceptance criterion.","failure":"注意干擾：以新孔量測代表舊孔會低估老化表面與燈具影響。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: New-tube measurements do not represent aged surfaces and lamps in the old tube. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b115-v14-27-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以同視角和乾濕條件比較兩孔的光度量測。以駕駛視角的亮度量測配合照度網格，分別檢查乾濕路面與燈具衰減，保留外部天空條件。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Compare photometry in both tubes under equal viewing and wetness conditions. Combine driver-view luminance with illuminance grids, checking dry and wet pavement and lamp depreciation while preserving exterior sky conditions. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b115-v14-27-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「漫反射亮度」的交付需回答：以同視角和乾濕條件比較兩孔的光度量測。將視角、路面狀態和光度校正連同量測交付，照明調整需按核准場景測試，不把理想反射公式當驗收標準。","textEn":"For Frejus Road Tunnel, the diffuse luminance handover must address the following evidence: Compare photometry in both tubes under equal viewing and wetness conditions. Hand over viewing geometry, pavement state and photometric calibration; test changes against approved scenarios rather than treating ideal reflection as an acceptance criterion.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「視覺適應與路面亮度」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Visual adaptation and pavement luminance\"?","options":["以同視角和乾濕條件比較兩孔的光度量測。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、開挖序列與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","支護越厚越硬就一定能解決所有擠壓性地層。"],"optionsEn":["Compare photometry in both tubes under equal viewing and wetness conditions.","Temperature, water head, excavation sequence and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","Thicker and stiffer support necessarily solves every squeezing-ground problem."],"answer":0,"explanation":"以同視角和乾濕條件比較兩孔的光度量測。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Compare photometry in both tubes under equal viewing and wetness conditions. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":27},{"id":"b115-v14-28","title":"視覺適應與路面亮度：失效診斷","titleEn":"Visual adaptation and pavement luminance: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b115-v14-27"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「漫反射亮度」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Diffuse luminance” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"以新孔量測代表舊孔會低估老化表面與燈具影響。照度平均值合格仍可能存在低亮度障礙區或眩光，感測器沾污也會使調光系統低估外界亮度。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"New-tube measurements do not represent aged surfaces and lamps in the old tube. Acceptable average illuminance can coexist with dark obstacles or glare, while sensor contamination may bias adaptive lighting controls. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：路面反射、濕度、燈具配光及背景對比共同影響辨識；朗伯模型只示範理想漫反射，不能直接制定入口段燈具間距或真實道路安全值。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: A Lambertian model illustrates ideal diffuse reflection only; it cannot establish entrance-zone spacing or actual road-safety limits without photometric and operational assessment.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「照度越高就必然使隧道內所有物體更容易辨識。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Higher illuminance necessarily makes every tunnel object easier to detect.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b115-v14-28-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"以新孔量測代表舊孔會低估老化表面與燈具影響。照度平均值合格仍可能存在低亮度障礙區或眩光，感測器沾污也會使調光系統低估外界亮度。","textEn":"New-tube measurements do not represent aged surfaces and lamps in the old tube. Acceptable average illuminance can coexist with dark obstacles or glare, while sensor contamination may bias adaptive lighting controls.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b115-v14-28-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「視覺適應與路面亮度」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Visual adaptation and pavement luminance\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","以新孔量測代表舊孔會低估老化表面與燈具影響。","只要出口距離短，就不需要比較可用與所需安全時間。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","New-tube measurements do not represent aged surfaces and lamps in the old tube.","Short exit distance removes the need to compare available and required safe time."],"answer":1,"explanation":"以新孔量測代表舊孔會低估老化表面與燈具影響。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"New-tube measurements do not represent aged surfaces and lamps in the old tube. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":28},{"id":"b115-v14-29","title":"疏散時間與分區可用性：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Evacuation time and zone availability: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b115-v14-28"],"objective":"說明「所需疏散時間」如何影響弗雷瑞斯公路隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Required evacuation time” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Frejus Road Tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"跨孔撤離先確認鄰孔交通已處於受控狀態，教材將橫通道距離與安全孔可用性分開。疏散時間包含辨識、反應、移動及排隊，不只由出口距離決定。人員速度會受煙熱、能見度及行動能力影響，安全判斷還要比較可用安全時間；橫通道存在但門或鄰孔不可用時，圖上的最短路線不一定能作實際選擇。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「所需疏散時間」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Cross-bore evacuation first requires a controlled receiving tube; separate passage distance from receiving-bore availability. Evacuation includes detection, response, travel and queues, not merely distance to an exit. Smoke, visibility and mobility alter walking speed, while safety requires comparison with available safe time. A passage shown on a plan may be unusable because its door or receiving bore is unavailable, invalidating the nominal shortest route. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Required evacuation time” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：前置時間=108 s；行走距離=340 m；行走速度=0.8 m/s。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: pre-movement time=108 s; travel distance=340 m; walking speed=0.8 m/s.","failure":"常見誤解：「只要出口距離短，就不需要比較可用與所需安全時間。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Short exit distance removes the need to compare available and required safe time.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「所需疏散時間」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Required evacuation time”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b115-v14-29-k1","title":"疏散時間與分區可用性","titleEn":"Evacuation time and zone availability","text":"跨孔撤離先確認鄰孔交通已處於受控狀態，教材將橫通道距離與安全孔可用性分開。疏散時間包含辨識、反應、移動及排隊，不只由出口距離決定。","textEn":"Cross-bore evacuation first requires a controlled receiving tube; separate passage distance from receiving-bore availability. Evacuation includes detection, response, travel and queues, not merely distance to an exit.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b115-v14-29-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：只要出口距離短，就不需要比較可用與所需安全時間。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Short exit distance removes the need to compare available and required safe time. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「疏散時間與分區可用性」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Evacuation time and zone availability\" is correct?","options":["只要出口距離短，就不需要比較可用與所需安全時間。","設備有兩台就可以直接把各自故障率相乘判定安全。","跨孔撤離先確認鄰孔交通已處於受控狀態，教材將橫通道距離與安全孔可用性分開。"],"optionsEn":["Short exit distance removes the need to compare available and required safe time.","Two units allow their failure probabilities to be multiplied directly to establish safety.","Cross-bore evacuation first requires a controlled receiving tube; separate passage distance from receiving-bore availability."],"answer":2,"explanation":"跨孔撤離先確認鄰孔交通已處於受控狀態，教材將橫通道距離與安全孔可用性分開。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Cross-bore evacuation first requires a controlled receiving tube; separate passage distance from receiving-bore availability. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":29},{"id":"b115-v14-30","title":"疏散時間與分區可用性：定量估算","titleEn":"Evacuation time and zone availability: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b115-v14-29"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「所需疏散時間」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Required evacuation time” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：前置時間=108 s；行走距離=340 m；行走速度=0.8 m/s。RSET=tpre+d/v=533 s。僅把行走距離增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為575.5 s。邊界：單群體固定速度，不含排隊煙熱及能力差異，不能單獨判安全；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: pre-movement time=108 s; travel distance=340 m; walking speed=0.8 m/s. RSET=tpre+d/v=533 s. Increasing only travel distance by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 575.5 s. Boundary: One group at fixed speed without queues, smoke or mobility differences; not a safety conclusion. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：演練同步核對交通隔離、門位和人員到達時間。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Exercise traffic isolation, door state and arrival timing together.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b115-v14-30-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：前置時間=108 s；行走距離=340 m；行走速度=0.8 m/s。RSET=tpre+d/v=533 s。僅把行走距離增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為575.5 s。邊界：單群體固定速度，不含排隊煙熱及能力差異，不能單獨判安全；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: pre-movement time=108 s; travel distance=340 m; walking speed=0.8 m/s. RSET=tpre+d/v=533 s. Increasing only travel distance by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 575.5 s. Boundary: One group at fixed speed without queues, smoke or mobility differences; not a safety conclusion. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b115-v14-30-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「疏散時間與分區可用性」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Evacuation time and zone availability\", which statement holds?","options":["原創教學假設：前置時間=108 s；行走距離=340 m；行走速度=0.8 m/s。","最短的隧道路線一定也有最低施工與維護風險。","知道覆土深度就能唯一決定洞壁各方向的應力。"],"optionsEn":["Original teaching assumptions: pre-movement time=108 s; travel distance=340 m; walking speed=0.8 m/s.","The shortest tunnel alignment necessarily has the lowest construction and maintenance risk.","Cover depth uniquely determines wall stress in every direction."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創教學假設：前置時間=108 s；行走距離=340 m；行走速度=0.8 m/s。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: pre-movement time=108 s; travel distance=340 m; walking speed=0.8 m/s. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":30},{"id":"b115-v14-31","title":"疏散時間與分區可用性：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Evacuation time and zone availability: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b115-v14-30"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「所需疏散時間」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Required evacuation time” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"演練同步核對交通隔離、門位和人員到達時間。以人流模擬或受控演練分辨前置時間、行走與門口排隊，核對每個出口接收區的可用狀態及通訊紀錄。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Exercise traffic isolation, door state and arrival timing together. Separate pre-movement, travel and doorway queues through simulation or controlled drills, checking receiving-zone availability and communication records for each exit. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「所需疏散時間」的交付需回答：演練同步核對交通隔離、門位和人員到達時間。疏散模型保留人口、速度分布及出口狀態，演練改動由營運與防災責任者批准，教材算例不得當作現場指揮程序。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Frejus Road Tunnel, the required evacuation time handover must address the following evidence: Exercise traffic isolation, door state and arrival timing together. Retain population, speed distribution and exit states; operations and fire-safety owners approve drill changes, and classroom calculations are not incident-command procedures.","failure":"注意干擾：橫通道到達快不代表鄰孔車流已安全停止。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Fast passage arrival does not establish stopped traffic in the receiving bore. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b115-v14-31-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"演練同步核對交通隔離、門位和人員到達時間。以人流模擬或受控演練分辨前置時間、行走與門口排隊，核對每個出口接收區的可用狀態及通訊紀錄。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Exercise traffic isolation, door state and arrival timing together. Separate pre-movement, travel and doorway queues through simulation or controlled drills, checking receiving-zone availability and communication records for each exit. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b115-v14-31-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「所需疏散時間」的交付需回答：演練同步核對交通隔離、門位和人員到達時間。疏散模型保留人口、速度分布及出口狀態，演練改動由營運與防災責任者批准，教材算例不得當作現場指揮程序。","textEn":"For Frejus Road Tunnel, the required evacuation time handover must address the following evidence: Exercise traffic isolation, door state and arrival timing together. Retain population, speed distribution and exit states; operations and fire-safety owners approve drill changes, and classroom calculations are not incident-command procedures.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「疏散時間與分區可用性」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Evacuation time and zone availability\"?","options":["沿用另一條隧道或另一處地層的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","演練同步核對交通隔離、門位和人員到達時間。","混凝土強度達標就不必檢查接縫轉動與偏壓。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another tunnel or ground formation counts as verifying this structure.","Exercise traffic isolation, door state and arrival timing together.","Passing concrete strength eliminates the need to check joint rotation and uneven pressure."],"answer":1,"explanation":"演練同步核對交通隔離、門位和人員到達時間。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Exercise traffic isolation, door state and arrival timing together. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":31},{"id":"b115-v14-32","title":"疏散時間與分區可用性：失效診斷","titleEn":"Evacuation time and zone availability: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b115-v14-31"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「所需疏散時間」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Required evacuation time” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"橫通道到達快不代表鄰孔車流已安全停止。以最快成人速度套全部旅客會低估需求，若忽略接收孔受煙或車流影響，疏散可能移到另一個危險邊界。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Fast passage arrival does not establish stopped traffic in the receiving bore. Applying the fastest adult speed to everyone understates demand; overlooking smoke or traffic in the receiving bore can transfer evacuees into another hazard. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：人員速度會受煙熱、能見度及行動能力影響，安全判斷還要比較可用安全時間；橫通道存在但門或鄰孔不可用時，圖上的最短路線不一定能作實際選擇。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: A passage shown on a plan may be unusable because its door or receiving bore is unavailable, invalidating the nominal shortest route.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「只要出口距離短，就不需要比較可用與所需安全時間。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Short exit distance removes the need to compare available and required safe time.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b115-v14-32-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"橫通道到達快不代表鄰孔車流已安全停止。以最快成人速度套全部旅客會低估需求，若忽略接收孔受煙或車流影響，疏散可能移到另一個危險邊界。","textEn":"Fast passage arrival does not establish stopped traffic in the receiving bore. Applying the fastest adult speed to everyone understates demand; overlooking smoke or traffic in the receiving bore can transfer evacuees into another hazard.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b115-v14-32-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「疏散時間與分區可用性」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Evacuation time and zone availability\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","設備有兩台就可以直接把各自故障率相乘判定安全。","橫通道到達快不代表鄰孔車流已安全停止。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","Two units allow their failure probabilities to be multiplied directly to establish safety.","Fast passage arrival does not establish stopped traffic in the receiving bore."],"answer":2,"explanation":"橫通道到達快不代表鄰孔車流已安全停止。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Fast passage arrival does not establish stopped traffic in the receiving bore. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":32}],"order":4},{"id":"b115-v14-s5","title":"耐久、維護與工程交接","titleEn":"Durability, maintenance and engineering handoff","description":"本階段聚焦「設備備援與共同失效」與「資產編碼與可追溯交接」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Equipment redundancy and common failure\" and \"Asset identity and traceable handover\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b115-v14-33","title":"設備備援與共同失效：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Equipment redundancy and common failure: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b115-v14-32"],"objective":"說明「系統不可用率」如何影響弗雷瑞斯公路隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “System unavailability” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Frejus Road Tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"兩孔控制若共享通訊骨幹，表面設備成雙仍可能共同失效，研究切換與隔離的測試範圍。兩套設備只有在故障近似獨立且切換可靠時，並聯才顯著降低不可用率。共用配電、控制軟體、冷卻或受淹位置會把獨立假設破壞；維修停用也改變當下配置，因此可靠度模型必須明列共有資源和設備狀態，不能只數備用台數。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「系統不可用率」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Shared communications can defeat apparent twin-bore redundancy; examine the scope of transfer and isolation tests. Parallel equipment sharply reduces unavailability only when failures are approximately independent and transfer works. Shared power, software, cooling or flood exposure breaks that assumption. Planned maintenance also changes the available configuration, so reliability models must identify shared resources and states rather than count spare units or multiply unsupported independent probabilities. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “System unavailability” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：單機不可用率=0.024 無因次。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: single-unit unavailability=0.024 dimensionless.","failure":"常見誤解：「設備有兩台就可以直接把各自故障率相乘判定安全。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Two units allow their failure probabilities to be multiplied directly to establish safety.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「系統不可用率」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “System unavailability”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b115-v14-33-k1","title":"設備備援與共同失效","titleEn":"Equipment redundancy and common failure","text":"兩孔控制若共享通訊骨幹，表面設備成雙仍可能共同失效，研究切換與隔離的測試範圍。兩套設備只有在故障近似獨立且切換可靠時，並聯才顯著降低不可用率。","textEn":"Shared communications can defeat apparent twin-bore redundancy; examine the scope of transfer and isolation tests. Parallel equipment sharply reduces unavailability only when failures are approximately independent and transfer works.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b115-v14-33-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：設備有兩台就可以直接把各自故障率相乘判定安全。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Two units allow their failure probabilities to be multiplied directly to establish safety. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「設備備援與共同失效」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Equipment redundancy and common failure\" is correct?","options":["兩孔控制若共享通訊骨幹，表面設備成雙仍可能共同失效，研究切換與隔離的測試範圍。","設備有兩台就可以直接把各自故障率相乘判定安全。","全部檔案上傳完成就代表工程交接已經驗收合格。"],"optionsEn":["Shared communications can defeat apparent twin-bore redundancy; examine the scope of transfer and isolation tests.","Two units allow their failure probabilities to be multiplied directly to establish safety.","Uploading all files means that engineering handover has been accepted."],"answer":0,"explanation":"兩孔控制若共享通訊骨幹，表面設備成雙仍可能共同失效，研究切換與隔離的測試範圍。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Shared communications can defeat apparent twin-bore redundancy; examine the scope of transfer and isolation tests. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":33},{"id":"b115-v14-34","title":"設備備援與共同失效：定量估算","titleEn":"Equipment redundancy and common failure: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b115-v14-33"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「系統不可用率」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “System unavailability” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：單機不可用率=0.024 無因次。Uparallel=U²=0.000576 probability。僅把單機不可用率增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為0.00069696 probability。邊界：完全獨立並聯與完美切換，不含共同失效；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: single-unit unavailability=0.024 dimensionless. Uparallel=U²=0.000576 probability. Increasing only single-unit unavailability by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 0.00069696 probability. Boundary: Independent parallel units with perfect transfer, excluding common failures. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：追查兩孔感測、控制和供電的共同節點。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Trace shared sensing, control and power nodes across both bores.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b115-v14-34-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：單機不可用率=0.024 無因次。Uparallel=U²=0.000576 probability。僅把單機不可用率增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為0.00069696 probability。邊界：完全獨立並聯與完美切換，不含共同失效；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: single-unit unavailability=0.024 dimensionless. Uparallel=U²=0.000576 probability. Increasing only single-unit unavailability by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 0.00069696 probability. Boundary: Independent parallel units with perfect transfer, excluding common failures. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b115-v14-34-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「設備備援與共同失效」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Equipment redundancy and common failure\", which statement holds?","options":["岩芯很硬就可以排除破碎帶變形與集中湧水。","原創教學假設：單機不可用率=0.024 無因次。","支護越厚越硬就一定能解決所有擠壓性地層。"],"optionsEn":["Hard intact core excludes fault-zone deformation and concentrated inflow.","Original teaching assumptions: single-unit unavailability=0.024 dimensionless.","Thicker and stiffer support necessarily solves every squeezing-ground problem."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創教學假設：單機不可用率=0.024 無因次。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: single-unit unavailability=0.024 dimensionless. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":34},{"id":"b115-v14-35","title":"設備備援與共同失效：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Equipment redundancy and common failure: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b115-v14-34"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「系統不可用率」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “System unavailability” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"追查兩孔感測、控制和供電的共同節點。由設備清單畫出故障樹，將電源、控制及實體位置追到共同節點，並用事件及維修紀錄檢查獨立假設。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Trace shared sensing, control and power nodes across both bores. Build a fault tree from the asset list, trace power, control and location to shared nodes, and test independence against incident and maintenance records. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「系統不可用率」的交付需回答：追查兩孔感測、控制和供電的共同節點。維修計畫附當日可用配置與剩餘備援，任何共同資源更動同步更新故障樹，切換試驗由設備及營運團隊共同見證。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Frejus Road Tunnel, the system unavailability handover must address the following evidence: Trace shared sensing, control and power nodes across both bores. Attach the actual configuration and remaining redundancy to maintenance plans, update fault trees after shared-resource changes, and witness transfer tests jointly.","failure":"注意干擾：只測單台停機不能揭露骨幹失效造成的雙孔影響。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Single-unit outage tests miss shared-backbone failure affecting both tubes. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b115-v14-35-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"追查兩孔感測、控制和供電的共同節點。由設備清單畫出故障樹，將電源、控制及實體位置追到共同節點，並用事件及維修紀錄檢查獨立假設。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Trace shared sensing, control and power nodes across both bores. Build a fault tree from the asset list, trace power, control and location to shared nodes, and test independence against incident and maintenance records. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b115-v14-35-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「系統不可用率」的交付需回答：追查兩孔感測、控制和供電的共同節點。維修計畫附當日可用配置與剩餘備援，任何共同資源更動同步更新故障樹，切換試驗由設備及營運團隊共同見證。","textEn":"For Frejus Road Tunnel, the system unavailability handover must address the following evidence: Trace shared sensing, control and power nodes across both bores. Attach the actual configuration and remaining redundancy to maintenance plans, update fault trees after shared-resource changes, and witness transfer tests jointly.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「設備備援與共同失效」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Equipment redundancy and common failure\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","風機銘牌風量相加就是全隧道各處可用的通風量。","追查兩孔感測、控制和供電的共同節點。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","Adding fan nameplate flows gives the usable airflow everywhere in the tunnel.","Trace shared sensing, control and power nodes across both bores."],"answer":2,"explanation":"追查兩孔感測、控制和供電的共同節點。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Trace shared sensing, control and power nodes across both bores. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":35},{"id":"b115-v14-36","title":"設備備援與共同失效：失效診斷","titleEn":"Equipment redundancy and common failure: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b115-v14-35"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「系統不可用率」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “System unavailability” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"只測單台停機不能揭露骨幹失效造成的雙孔影響。重複安裝卻共用單一供電可能在一次故障中全部停機，帳面可靠度很高但實際不可用時間沒有降低。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Single-unit outage tests miss shared-backbone failure affecting both tubes. Duplicated equipment on one supply can fail together in a single event, leaving actual downtime unchanged despite optimistic calculated reliability. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：共用配電、控制軟體、冷卻或受淹位置會把獨立假設破壞；維修停用也改變當下配置，因此可靠度模型必須明列共有資源和設備狀態，不能只數備用台數。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Planned maintenance also changes the available configuration, so reliability models must identify shared resources and states rather than count spare units or multiply unsupported independent probabilities.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「設備有兩台就可以直接把各自故障率相乘判定安全。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Two units allow their failure probabilities to be multiplied directly to establish safety.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b115-v14-36-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"只測單台停機不能揭露骨幹失效造成的雙孔影響。重複安裝卻共用單一供電可能在一次故障中全部停機，帳面可靠度很高但實際不可用時間沒有降低。","textEn":"Single-unit outage tests miss shared-backbone failure affecting both tubes. Duplicated equipment on one supply can fail together in a single event, leaving actual downtime unchanged despite optimistic calculated reliability.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b115-v14-36-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「設備備援與共同失效」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Equipment redundancy and common failure\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["只測單台停機不能揭露骨幹失效造成的雙孔影響。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","全部檔案上傳完成就代表工程交接已經驗收合格。"],"optionsEn":["Single-unit outage tests miss shared-backbone failure affecting both tubes.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","Uploading all files means that engineering handover has been accepted."],"answer":0,"explanation":"只測單台停機不能揭露骨幹失效造成的雙孔影響。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Single-unit outage tests miss shared-backbone failure affecting both tubes. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":36},{"id":"b115-v14-37","title":"資產編碼與可追溯交接：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Asset identity and traceable handover: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b115-v14-36"],"objective":"說明「資產資料完整度」如何影響弗雷瑞斯公路隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Asset-record completeness” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Frejus Road Tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"弗雷瑞斯版本交付應保留原孔和新孔獨立設備樹，避免複製名稱後遺失安裝日期及測試狀態。地下設備的竣工資料必須讓維護人員找到正確位置、材料批次和控制版本。只有上傳圖面而沒有變更歷程，無法分辨元件替換與真正劣化；告警、儀器、線路及工單使用一致識別碼，才可能把量測趨勢連回實際受力或水力系統。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「資產資料完整度」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Maintain separate asset trees for old and new tubes, preserving installation dates and test states when names are copied. Handover must let maintainers find the correct location, material batch and control revision. Drawings without change history cannot distinguish replacement from deterioration. Consistent identifiers across alarms, instruments, circuits and work orders are essential for linking trends to the physical structural or hydraulic system instead of treating each record as an isolated file. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Asset-record completeness” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：設備總數=114 個；缺紀錄數=16 個。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: asset count=114 count; missing records=16 count. coverage=100(N−missing)/N=85.9649 %.","failure":"常見誤解：「全部檔案上傳完成就代表工程交接已經驗收合格。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Uploading all files means that engineering handover has been accepted.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「資產資料完整度」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Asset-record completeness”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b115-v14-37-k1","title":"資產編碼與可追溯交接","titleEn":"Asset identity and traceable handover","text":"弗雷瑞斯版本交付應保留原孔和新孔獨立設備樹，避免複製名稱後遺失安裝日期及測試狀態。地下設備的竣工資料必須讓維護人員找到正確位置、材料批次和控制版本。","textEn":"Maintain separate asset trees for old and new tubes, preserving installation dates and test states when names are copied. Handover must let maintainers find the correct location, material batch and control revision.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b115-v14-37-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：全部檔案上傳完成就代表工程交接已經驗收合格。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Uploading all files means that engineering handover has been accepted. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「資產編碼與可追溯交接」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Asset identity and traceable handover\" is correct?","options":["全部檔案上傳完成就代表工程交接已經驗收合格。","弗雷瑞斯版本交付應保留原孔和新孔獨立設備樹，避免複製名稱後遺失安裝日期及測試狀態。","最短的隧道路線一定也有最低施工與維護風險。"],"optionsEn":["Uploading all files means that engineering handover has been accepted.","Maintain separate asset trees for old and new tubes, preserving installation dates and test states when names are copied.","The shortest tunnel alignment necessarily has the lowest construction and maintenance risk."],"answer":1,"explanation":"弗雷瑞斯版本交付應保留原孔和新孔獨立設備樹，避免複製名稱後遺失安裝日期及測試狀態。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Maintain separate asset trees for old and new tubes, preserving installation dates and test states when names are copied. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":37},{"id":"b115-v14-38","title":"資產編碼與可追溯交接：定量估算","titleEn":"Asset identity and traceable handover: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b115-v14-37"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「資產資料完整度」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Asset-record completeness” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：設備總數=114 個；缺紀錄數=16 個。coverage=100(N−missing)/N=85.9649 %。僅把缺紀錄數增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為84.5614 %。邊界：資料完整度，不等於安全或可靠度；擾動為連續敏感度，實際個數為整數；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: asset count=114 count; missing records=16 count. coverage=100(N−missing)/N=85.9649 %. Increasing only missing records by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 84.5614 %. Boundary: Record completeness, not safety or reliability; perturbation is continuous sensitivity while actual counts are integers. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：抽查同名設備是否有唯一孔別、位置和維護週期。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Check similarly named assets have unique bore, location and maintenance interval.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b115-v14-38-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：設備總數=114 個；缺紀錄數=16 個。coverage=100(N−missing)/N=85.9649 %。僅把缺紀錄數增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為84.5614 %。邊界：資料完整度，不等於安全或可靠度；擾動為連續敏感度，實際個數為整數；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: asset count=114 count; missing records=16 count. coverage=100(N−missing)/N=85.9649 %. Increasing only missing records by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 84.5614 %. Boundary: Record completeness, not safety or reliability; perturbation is continuous sensitivity while actual counts are integers. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b115-v14-38-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「資產編碼與可追溯交接」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Asset identity and traceable handover\", which statement holds?","options":["知道覆土深度就能唯一決定洞壁各方向的應力。","混凝土強度達標就不必檢查接縫轉動與偏壓。","原創教學假設：設備總數=114 個；缺紀錄數=16 個。"],"optionsEn":["Cover depth uniquely determines wall stress in every direction.","Passing concrete strength eliminates the need to check joint rotation and uneven pressure.","Original teaching assumptions: asset count=114 count; missing records=16 count. coverage=100(N−missing)/N=85.9649 %."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設：設備總數=114 個；缺紀錄數=16 個。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: asset count=114 count; missing records=16 count. coverage=100(N−missing)/N=85.9649 %. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":38},{"id":"b115-v14-39","title":"資產編碼與可追溯交接：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Asset identity and traceable handover: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b115-v14-38"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「資產資料完整度」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Asset-record completeness” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"抽查同名設備是否有唯一孔別、位置和維護週期。抽取一條告警，從控制畫面追到設備、線路、圖面和工單，核對位置、版本及校正日期並記錄無法閉合的欄位。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Check similarly named assets have unique bore, location and maintenance interval. Trace a sampled alarm from screen to equipment, circuit, drawing and work order, checking location, revision and calibration dates and recording broken links. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「資產資料完整度」的交付需回答：抽查同名設備是否有唯一孔別、位置和維護週期。交接以可完成的定位、查找與復原任務驗證，由維護責任人確認現場可用性；完整度只是資料指標，不代表結構安全或設備可靠。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Frejus Road Tunnel, the asset-record completeness handover must address the following evidence: Check similarly named assets have unique bore, location and maintenance interval. Validate handover through achievable location, retrieval and recovery tasks witnessed by maintainers; completeness measures records, not structural safety or equipment reliability.","failure":"注意干擾：錯把新孔測試結果覆蓋舊孔會形成虛假的驗收證據。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Overwriting old-bore records with new-bore tests creates false acceptance evidence. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b115-v14-39-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"抽查同名設備是否有唯一孔別、位置和維護週期。抽取一條告警，從控制畫面追到設備、線路、圖面和工單，核對位置、版本及校正日期並記錄無法閉合的欄位。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Check similarly named assets have unique bore, location and maintenance interval. Trace a sampled alarm from screen to equipment, circuit, drawing and work order, checking location, revision and calibration dates and recording broken links. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b115-v14-39-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「資產資料完整度」的交付需回答：抽查同名設備是否有唯一孔別、位置和維護週期。交接以可完成的定位、查找與復原任務驗證，由維護責任人確認現場可用性；完整度只是資料指標，不代表結構安全或設備可靠。","textEn":"For Frejus Road Tunnel, the asset-record completeness handover must address the following evidence: Check similarly named assets have unique bore, location and maintenance interval. Validate handover through achievable location, retrieval and recovery tasks witnessed by maintainers; completeness measures records, not structural safety or equipment reliability.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「資產編碼與可追溯交接」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Asset identity and traceable handover\"?","options":["抽查同名設備是否有唯一孔別、位置和維護週期。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","照度越高就必然使隧道內所有物體更容易辨識。"],"optionsEn":["Check similarly named assets have unique bore, location and maintenance interval.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","Higher illuminance necessarily makes every tunnel object easier to detect."],"answer":0,"explanation":"抽查同名設備是否有唯一孔別、位置和維護週期。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Check similarly named assets have unique bore, location and maintenance interval. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":39},{"id":"b115-v14-40","title":"資產編碼與可追溯交接：失效診斷","titleEn":"Asset identity and traceable handover: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b115-v14-39"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「資產資料完整度」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Asset-record completeness” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"錯把新孔測試結果覆蓋舊孔會形成虛假的驗收證據。設備改名卻未更新控制畫面會引導人員隔離錯誤回路，材料批次缺漏則使同批缺陷無法追蹤到其他位置。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Overwriting old-bore records with new-bore tests creates false acceptance evidence. Renaming an asset without updating the screen can isolate the wrong circuit; missing material batches prevent tracing related defects at other locations. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：只有上傳圖面而沒有變更歷程，無法分辨元件替換與真正劣化；告警、儀器、線路及工單使用一致識別碼，才可能把量測趨勢連回實際受力或水力系統。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Consistent identifiers across alarms, instruments, circuits and work orders are essential for linking trends to the physical structural or hydraulic system instead of treating each record as an isolated file.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「全部檔案上傳完成就代表工程交接已經驗收合格。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Uploading all files means that engineering handover has been accepted.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b115-v14-40-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"錯把新孔測試結果覆蓋舊孔會形成虛假的驗收證據。設備改名卻未更新控制畫面會引導人員隔離錯誤回路，材料批次缺漏則使同批缺陷無法追蹤到其他位置。","textEn":"Overwriting old-bore records with new-bore tests creates false acceptance evidence. Renaming an asset without updating the screen can isolate the wrong circuit; missing material batches prevent tracing related defects at other locations.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b115-v14-40-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「資產編碼與可追溯交接」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Asset identity and traceable handover\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","錯把新孔測試結果覆蓋舊孔會形成虛假的驗收證據。","最短的隧道路線一定也有最低施工與維護風險。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Overwriting old-bore records with new-bore tests creates false acceptance evidence.","The shortest tunnel alignment necessarily has the lowest construction and maintenance risk."],"answer":1,"explanation":"錯把新孔測試結果覆蓋舊孔會形成虛假的驗收證據。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Overwriting old-bore records with new-bore tests creates false acceptance evidence. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":40}],"order":5}],"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b115","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"curriculumVersion":14,"stepCount":40,"estimatedMinutes":1000}};
